    ns1:description """# Swedish Earth Biogenome Project - Genome Assembly Workflow\r
\r
The primary genome assembly workflow for the Earth Biogenome Project at NBIS.\r
\r
## Workflow overview\r
\r
General aim:\r
\r
```mermaid\r
flowchart LR\r
    hifi[/ HiFi reads /] --> data_inspection\r
    ont[/ ONT reads /] -->  data_inspection\r
    hic[/ Hi-C reads /] --> data_inspection\r
    data_inspection[[ Data inspection ]] --> preprocessing\r
    preprocessing[[ Preprocessing ]] --> assemble\r
    assemble[[ Assemble ]] --> validation\r
    validation[[ Assembly validation ]] --> curation\r
    curation[[ Assembly curation ]] --> validation\r
```\r
\r
Current implementation:\r
\r
```mermaid\r
flowchart TD\r
    input[/ Input file/] --> hifi\r
    input --> hic\r
    input --> taxonkit[[ TaxonKit name2taxid/reformat ]]\r
    taxonkit --> goat_taxon[[ GOAT taxon search ]]\r
    goat_taxon --> busco\r
    goat_taxon --> dtol[[ DToL lookup ]]\r
    hifi --> samtools_fa[[ Samtools fasta ]]\r
    samtools_fa --> fastk_hifi\r
    samtools_fa --> mash_screen\r
    hifi[/ HiFi reads /] --> fastk_hifi[[ FastK - HiFi ]]\r
    hifi --> meryl_hifi[[ Meryl - HiFi ]]\r
    hic[/ Hi-C reads /] --> fastk_hic[[ FastK - Hi-C ]]\r
    hifi --> meryl_hic[[ Meryl - Hi-C ]]\r
    assembly[/ Assembly /] --> quast[[ Quast ]]\r
    fastk_hifi --> histex[[ Histex ]]\r
    histex --> genescopefk[[ GeneScopeFK ]]\r
    fastk_hifi --> ploidyplot[[ PloidyPlot ]]\r
    fastk_hifi --> katgc[[ KatGC ]]\r
    fastk_hifi --> merquryfk[[ MerquryFK ]]\r
    assembly --> merquryfk\r
    meryl_hifi --> merqury[[ Merqury ]]\r
    assembly --> merqury\r
    fastk_hifi --> katcomp[[ KatComp ]]\r
    fastk_hic --> katcomp\r
    assembly --> busco[[ Busco ]]\r
    refseq_sketch[( RefSeq sketch )] --> mash_screen[[ Mash Screen ]]\r
    hifi --> mash_screen\r
    fastk_hifi --> hifiasm[[ HiFiasm ]]\r
    hifiasm --> assembly\r
    assembly --> purgedups[[ Purgedups ]]\r
    input --> mitoref[[ Mitohifi - Find reference ]]\r
    assembly --> mitohifi[[ Mitohifi ]]\r
    assembly --> fcsgx[[ FCS GX ]]\r
    fcs_fetchdb[( FCS fetchdb )] --> fcsgx\r
    mitoref --> mitohifi\r
    genescopefk --> quarto[[ Quarto ]]\r
    goat_taxon --> multiqc[[ MultiQC ]]\r
    quarto --> multiqc\r
    dtol --> multiqc\r
    katgc --> multiqc\r
    ploidyplot --> multiqc\r
    busco --> multiqc\r
    quast --> multiqc\r
```\r
\r
## Usage\r
\r
```bash\r
nextflow run -params-file <params.yml> \\\r
    [ -c <custom.config> ] \\\r
    [ -profile <profile> ] \\\r
    NBISweden/Earth-Biogenome-Project-pilot\r
```\r
\r
where:\r
- `params.yml` is a YAML formatted file containing workflow parameters\r
    such as input paths to the assembly specification, and settings for tools within the workflow.\r
\r
    Example:\r
\r
    ```yml\r
    input: 'assembly_spec.yml'\r
    outdir: results\r
    fastk: # Optional\r
      kmer_size: 31 # default 31\r
    genescopefk: # Optional\r
      kmer_size: 31 # default 31\r
    hifiasm: # Optional, default = no extra options: Key (e.g. 'opts01') is used in assembly build name (e.g., 'hifiasm-raw-opts01').\r
      opts01: "--opts A"\r
      opts02: "--opts B"\r
    busco: # Optional, default: retrieved from GOAT\r
      lineages: 'auto' # comma separated string of lineages or auto.\r
    ```\r
\r
    Alternatively parameters can be provided on the\r
    command-line using the `--parameter` notation (e.g., `--input <path>` ).\r
- `<custom.config>` is a Nextflow configuration file which provides\r
    additional configuration. This is used to customise settings other than\r
    workflow parameters, such as cpus, time, and command-line options to tools.\r
\r
    Example:\r
    ```nextflow\r
    process {\r
        withName: 'BUSCO' {  // Selects the process to apply settings.\r
            cpus     = 6     // Overrides cpu settings defined in nextflow.config\r
            time     = 4.d   // Overrides time settings defined in nextflow.config to 4 days. Use .h for hours, .m for minutes.\r
            memory   = '20GB'  // Overrides memory settings defined in nextflow.config to 20 GB.\r
            // ext.args supplies command-line options to the process tool\r
            // overrides settings found in configs/modules.config\r
            ext.args = '--long'  // Supplies these as command-line options to Busco\r
        }\r
    }\r
    ```\r
- `<profile>` is one of the preconfigured execution profiles\r
    (`uppmax`, `singularity_local`, `docker_local`, etc: see nextflow.config). Alternatively,\r
    you can provide a custom configuration to configure this workflow\r
    to your execution environment. See [Nextflow Configuration](https://www.nextflow.io/docs/latest/config.html#scope-executor)\r
    for more details.\r
\r
\r
### Workflow parameter inputs\r
\r
Mandatory:\r
\r
- `input`: A YAML formatted input file.\r
    Example `assembly_spec.yml` (See also [test profile input](assets/test_hsapiens.yml) TODO:: Update test profile):\r
\r
    ```yml\r
    sample:                          # Required: Meta data\r
      name: 'Laetiporus sulphureus'  # Required: Species name. Correct spelling is important to look up species information.\r
      ploidy: 2                      # Optional: Estimated ploidy (default: retrieved from GOAT)\r
      genome_size: 2345              # Optional: Estimated genome size (default: retrieved from GOAT)\r
      haploid_number: 13             # Optional: Estimated haploid chromosome count (default: retrieved from GOAT)\r
      taxid: 5630                    # Optional: Taxon ID (default: retrieved with Taxonkit)\r
      kingdom: Eukaryota             # Optional: (default: retrived with Taxonkit)\r
    assembly:                        # Optional: List of assemblies to curate and validate.\r
      - assembler: hifiasm           # For each entry, the assembler,\r
        stage: raw                   # stage of assembly,\r
        id: uuid                     # unique id,\r
        pri_fasta: /path/to/primary_asm.fasta # and paths to sequences are required.\r
        alt_fasta: /path/to/alternate_asm.fasta\r
        pri_gfa: /path/to/primary_asm.gfa\r
        alt_gfa: /path/to/alternate_asm.gfa\r
      - assembler: ipa\r
        stage: raw\r
        id: uuid\r
        pri_fasta: /path/to/primary_asm.fasta\r
        alt_fasta: /path/to/alternate_asm.fasta\r
    hic:                             # Optional: List of hi-c reads to QC and use for scaffolding\r
      - read1: '/path/to/raw/data/hic/LS_HIC_R001_1.fastq.gz'\r
        read2: '/path/to/raw/data/hic/LS_HIC_R001_2.fastq.gz'\r
    hifi:                            # Required: List of hifi-reads to QC and use for assembly/validation\r
      - reads: '/path/to/raw/data/hifi/LS_HIFI_R001.bam'\r
    rnaseq:                          # Optional: List of Rna-seq reads to use for validation\r
      - read1: '/path/to/raw/data/rnaseq/LS_RNASEQ_R001_1.fastq.gz'\r
        read2: '/path/to/raw/data/rnaseq/LS_RNASEQ_R001_2.fastq.gz'\r
    isoseq:                          # Optional: List of Isoseq reads to use for validation\r
      - reads: '/path/to/raw/data/isoseq/LS_ISOSEQ_R001.bam'\r
    ```\r
\r
\r
Optional:\r
\r
- `outdir`: The publishing path for results (default: `results`).\r
- `publish_mode`: (values: `'symlink'` (default), `'copy'`) The file\r
publishing method from the intermediate results folders\r
(see [Table of publish modes](https://www.nextflow.io/docs/latest/process.html#publishdir)).\r
- `steps`: The workflow steps to execute (default is all steps). Choose from:\r
\r
    - `inspect`: 01 - Read inspection\r
    - `preprocess`: 02 - Read preprocessing\r
    - `assemble`: 03 - Assembly\r
    - `purge`: 04 - Duplicate purging\r
    - `polish`: 05 - Error polishing\r
    - `screen`: 06 - Contamination screening\r
    - `scaffold`: 07 - Scaffolding\r
    - `curate`: 08 - Rapid curation\r
    - `alignRNA`: 09 - Align RNAseq data\r
\r
Software specific:\r
\r
Tool specific settings are provided by supplying values to specific keys or supplying an array of\r
settings under a tool name. The input to `-params-file` would look like this:\r
\r
```yml\r
input: assembly.yml\r
outdir: results\r
fastk:\r
  kmer_size: 31\r
genescopefk:\r
  kmer_size: 31\r
hifiasm:\r
  opts01: "--opts A"\r
  opts02: "--opts B"\r
busco:\r
  lineages: 'auto'\r
```\r
\r
- `multiqc_config`: Path to MultiQC configuration file (default: `configs/multiqc_conf.yaml`).\r
\r
Uppmax and PDC cluster specific:\r
\r
- `project`: NAISS Compute allocation number.\r
\r
### Workflow outputs\r
\r
All results are published to the path assigned to the workflow parameter `results`.\r
\r
TODO:: List folder contents in results file\r
### Customization for Uppmax\r
\r
A custom profile named `uppmax` is available to run this workflow specifically\r
on UPPMAX clusters. The process `executor` is `slurm` so jobs are\r
submitted to the Slurm Queue Manager. All jobs submitted to slurm\r
must have a project allocation. This is automatically added to the `clusterOptions`\r
in the `uppmax` profile. All Uppmax clusters have node local disk space to do\r
computations, and prevent heavy input/output over the network (which\r
slows down the cluster for all).\r
The path to this disk space is provided by the `$SNIC_TMP` variable, used by\r
the `process.scratch` directive in the `uppmax` profile. Lastly\r
the profile enables the use of Singularity so that all processes must be\r
executed within Singularity containers. See [nextflow.config](nextflow.config)\r
for the profile specification.\r
\r
The profile is enabled using the `-profile` parameter to nextflow:\r
```bash\r
nextflow run -profile uppmax <nextflow_script>\r
```\r
\r
A NAISS compute allocation should also be supplied using the `--project` parameter.\r
\r
### Customization for PDC\r
\r
A custom profile named `dardel` is available to run this workflow specifically\r
on the PDC cluster *Dardel*. The process `executor` is `slurm` so jobs are\r
submitted to the Slurm Queue Manager. All jobs submitted to slurm\r
must have a project allocation. This is automatically added to the `clusterOptions`\r
in the `dardel` profile. Calculations are performed in the scratch space allocated\r
by `PDC_TMP` which is also on the lustre file system and is not node local storage.\r
The path to this disk space is provided by the `$PDC_TMP` variable, used by\r
the `process.scratch` directive in the `dardel` profile. Lastly\r
the profile enables the use of Singularity so that all processes must be\r
executed within Singularity containers. See [nextflow.config](nextflow.config)\r
for the profile specification.\r
\r
The profile is enabled using the `-profile` parameter to nextflow:\r
```bash\r
nextflow run -profile dardel <nextflow_script>\r
```\r
\r
A NAISS compute allocation should also be supplied using the `--project` parameter.\r
\r
## Workflow organization\r
\r
The workflows in this folder manage the execution of your analyses\r
from beginning to end.\r
\r
```\r
workflow/\r
 | - .github/                        Github data such as actions to run\r
 | - assets/                         Workflow assets such as test samplesheets\r
 | - bin/                            Custom workflow scripts\r
 | - configs/                        Configuration files that govern workflow execution\r
 | - dockerfiles/                    Custom container definition files\r
 | - docs/                           Workflow usage and interpretation information\r
 | - modules/                        Process definitions for tools used in the workflow\r
 | - subworkflows/                   Custom workflows for different stages of the main analysis\r
 | - tests/                          Workflow tests\r
 | - main.nf                         The primary analysis script\r
 | - nextflow.config                 General Nextflow configuration\r
 \\ - modules.json                    nf-core file which tracks modules/subworkflows from nf-core\r
```\r
\r
""" ;
    ns1:featureList <http://edamontology.org/operation_0296>,
