<https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/1125?version=1> a ns1:ComputationalWorkflow ;
    dcterms:conformsTo "https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalWorkflow/1.0-RELEASE" ;
    ns1:applicationSubCategory <http://edamontology.org/topic_0091> ;
    ns1:citation "10.48546/workflowhub.workflow.1125.1" ;
    ns1:creator "Pavel Akhtyamov" ;
    ns1:dateCreated "2024-09-05" ;
    ns1:dateModified "2026-05-13" ;
    ns1:description """# Article-GADES\r
\r
This repository represents generating and benchmarking the results of the [GADES](https://github.com/lab-medvedeva/GADES-main) package for Distance Matrix Calculation\r
\r
## Installation\r
\r
```shell\r
git lfs install\r
git clone https://github.com/lab-medvedeva/Article-GADES.git\r
cd Article-GADES\r
```\r
\r
Put the Real datasets in the MEX format to the folder `Datasets/Real`.\r
\r
### Running benchmark using Docker Deployment\r
```shell\r
docker run --gpus all \\\r
    -v $PWD/Datasets:/workspace/Article-GADES/Datasets \\\r
    -v $PWD/results:/workspace/Article-GADES/results \\\r
    akhtyamovpavel/article-gades \r
```\r
\r
## Step 01. Generation of the datasets\r
\r
### Step 01.1. Generated Dense Datasets\r
\r
```shell\r
cd ./scripts/MatricesGeneration\r
./generate_dense.sh ../../Datasets/\r
```\r
\r
### Step 01.2. Generated Sparse Datasets\r
\r
```shell\r
cd ./scripts/MatricesGeneration\r
./generate_sparse.sh ../../Datasets/\r
```\r
\r
## Step 02. Benchmarking\r
\r
### Step 02.1. Generated Dense Datasets\r
```shell\r
cd ./scripts/Benchmarking\r
\r
./run_benchmark_generated_dense.sh ../../\r
\r
./run_benchmark_python_dense.sh ../../\r
```\r
\r
### Step 02.2. Generated Sparse Datasets\r
\r
```shell\r
\r
cd ./scripts/Benchmarking/\r
\r
./run_benchmark_generated_sparse.sh ../../\r
```\r
\r
### Step 02.3 Real Datasets\r
```shell\r
\r
cd ./Scripts/Benchmarking/\r
./run_benchmark_real_python.sh <path to dataset> ../../results/RealDatasets/<name of the real dataset>/\r
./run_benchmark_real_R.sh <path to dataset> ../../results/RealDatasets/<name of the dataset>/\r
```\r
\r
Example:\r
```shell\r
./run_benchmark.sh ../../Datasets/Real/HLCA_marrow.mtx ../results/RealDatasets/HLCA_marrow/\r
```\r
\r
\r
### Step 02.4. Ablation Study for the Batch Size Usage\r
\r
### Step 02.5. Ablation Study for the Memory Usage\r
```\r
cd ./Scripts/Benchmarking\r
./run_benchmark_real_python_memory_usage.sh <path to dataset> ../../results/RealDatasetsBatchSizeFixedMemory/<name of the real dataset>/500/\r
```\r
\r
Example:\r
```\r
./run_benchmark_real_python_memory_usage.sh ../../Datasets/CellLines.mtx ../../results/RealDatasetsBatchSizeFixedMemory/CellLines/500/\r
```\r
\r
## Step 03. Drawing charts\r
\r
We split reproducibility notebooks into two parts:\r
* Aggregation over datasets\r
* Plotting charts\r
\r
### Aggregation\r
\r
1. For Generated Dense datasets you could use the [GeneratedDatasetsCollector](/reproducibility/00-GeneratedDatasetsCollector.ipynb) notebook.\r
2. For Generated Sparse datasets you could use the [GeneratedSparseCollector](/reproducibility/00-GeneratedSparseCollector.ipynb) notebook.\r
\r
### Analyzing datasets\r
\r
1. Generated datasets analyzed in the [GeneratedDatasetAnalysis](/reproducibility/GeneratedDatasetAnalysis.ipynb) notebook.\r
2. Real datasets analyzed in the [RealDatasetAnalysis](/reproducibility/RealDatasetsAnalysis.ipynb) notebook.\r
3. Analysis of ablation study could be found in the [reproducibility](/reproducibility/03-AblationStudy.ipynb) notebook.\r
""" ;
    ns1:featureList <http://edamontology.org/operation_0289>,
        <http://edamontology.org/operation_3465> ;
