<https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/1160?version=2> a ns1:ComputationalWorkflow ;
    dcterms:conformsTo "https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalWorkflow/1.0-RELEASE" ;
    ns1:citation "10.48546/workflowhub.workflow.1160.2" ;
    ns1:creator "Leverages scripts developed by Weber et al (2021) DOI: https://doi.org/10.1093/gigascience/giab062",
        "Michael Lynch" ;
    ns1:dateCreated "2024-09-16" ;
    ns1:dateModified "2026-05-13" ;
    ns1:description """# demux_doublet_sim\r
\r
Repository for Nextflow pipeline used in demuxSNP demultipelxing paper\r
\r
## Overall workflow\r
\r
1. Simulate doublets\r
- Add per-sample suffix to barcodes in BAM\r
- Merge per-sample BAMs\r
- Generate lookup of barcodes to rename to reach a set % doublets\r
-  Rename barcodes in BAM as per lookup\r
2. Benchmark methods\r
- Experiments 1: Vary doublet rate\r
- Experiment 2: Vary SNP subsetting\r
\r
## Inputs\r
\r
Most inputs are specified in nextflow.config:\r
    container__souporcell: path to souporcell apptainer image, ideally at top level of project.  \r
    bam_path: Path to demultiplexed bam files.  \r
    barcodes_path: Path to demultiplexed barcodes.  \r
    tenx: Path to barcodes.tsv, features.tsv and matrix.mtx files from multiplexed 10X output.  \r
    common_variants: common variants e.g. from 1K genome project.  \r
    ref: path to reference genome, ideally in data/input directory.  \r
\r
Doublet simulation parameters are specified in params_ccrcc.csv\r
The workflow caters for subsampling (also specified in params_ccrcc.csv) although this was not explored in the paper.\r
\r
## Outputs\r
\r
Folder for each simulated scenario (e.g. seed, % doublets, number of genes used to subset)\r
SingleCellExperiment object in each demuxSNP folder.\r
\r
## Known issues\r
\r
Input files used by souporcell/apptainer need to be stored below the image.\r
Apptainer must be bound to the project directory (variable in nextflow.config).""" ;
    ns1:identifier "1160" ;
    ns1:license "CC-BY-4.0" ;
    ns1:name "Demultiplexing Doublet Benchmark" ;
    ns1:url <https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/1160?version=2> ;
    ns1:version "2" .

<https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/1161?version=1> a ns1:ComputationalWorkflow ;
    dcterms:conformsTo "https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalWorkflow/1.0-RELEASE" ;
    ns1:citation "10.48546/workflowhub.workflow.1161.1" ;
    ns1:creator "Jen-Hung Wang" ;
    ns1:dateCreated "2024-09-11" ;
    ns1:dateModified "2026-05-13" ;
    ns1:description """# **Stratum corneum nanotexture feature detection using deep learning and spatial analysis: a non-invasive tool for skin barrier assessment**\r
\r
<img src="./source/Overview.png" alt="Data Processing" width="95%" />\r
\r
This repository presents an objective, quantifiable method for assessing atopic dermatitis (AD) severity. The program integrates deep learning object detection with spatial analysis algorithms to accurately calculate the density of circular nano-size objects (CNOs), termed the Effective Corneocyte Topographical Index (ECTI). The ECTI demonstrates remarkable robustness in overcoming the inherent challenges of nano-imaging, such as environmental noise and structural occlusions on the corneocyte surface, further enhancing its applicability in clinical settings.\r
\r
## **Dependencies**\r
- Python 3.9+\r
- matplotlib\r
- numpy\r
- opencv-python\r
- scipy\r
- scikit-image\r
- ultralytics\r
- scikit-learn\r
- customtkinter\r
\r
## **Directories**\r
- `AD_Assessment_GUI.zip` contains a cross-platform executable GUI, sample data, and a tutorial video.\r
- `utils/Img_Preprocessing.py` demonstrates the image enhancement algorithms applied to the corneocyte nanotexture images.\r
\r
## **Usage**\r
1. Execution via cross-platform executable GUI\r
    - Download [AD_Assessment_GUI.zip](https://huggingface.co/jenhung/ECTI_Assessment_GUI)\r
    - Run `AD_Assessment_GUI.exe`\r
    - Analysis results will be saved within the selected path in a folder titled `CNO_Detection`\r
\r
2. Execution via python script\r
    - Install packages in terminal:\r
        ```    \r
        pip install -r requirements.txt\r
        ```\r
    - Run `AD_Assessment_GUI.py`\r
    - Analysis results will be saved within the selected path in a folder titled `CNO_Detection`\r
\r
## **Executable**\r
\r
1. Install PyInstaller in terminal:\r
                \r
    ```    \r
    pip install pyinstaller\r
    ```\r
   \r
2. Run command in terminal:\r
\r
    ```    \r
    pyinstaller --onedir .\\AD_Assessment_GUI.py\r
    ```\r
   \r
## **Performance**\r
\r
| Model                                                                | Test Size | #Parameter (M) | FLOPs (G) | AP<sup>50</sup> (%) | AP<sup>50-95</sup> (%) | Latency (ms) |\r
|:---------------------------------------------------------------------|:---------:|:--------------:|:---------:|:-------------------:|:----------------------:|:------------:|\r
| [YOLOv10-N](https://huggingface.co/jenhung/CNO_DETECTION_YOLOv8-L)   |    512    |      2.7       |    8.2    |        89.6         |          51.4          |     3.3      |\r
| [YOLOv10-S](https://huggingface.co/jenhung/CNO_DETECTION_YOLOv8-L)   |    512    |      8.0       |   24.4    |        90.8         |          55.5          |     4.58     |\r
| [YOLOv10-M](https://huggingface.co/jenhung/CNO_DETECTION_YOLOv8-L)   |    512    |      16.5      |   63.4    |        91.3         |          59.7          |     7.17     |\r
| [YOLOv10-B](https://huggingface.co/jenhung/CNO_DETECTION_YOLOv8-L)   |    512    |      20.4      |   97.7    |        91.1         |          62.5          |     7.58     |\r
| [YOLOv10-L](https://huggingface.co/jenhung/CNO_DETECTION_YOLOv8-L)   |    512    |      25.7      |   126.3   |        91.4         |          63.2          |     9.01     |\r
| [YOLOv10-X](https://huggingface.co/jenhung/CNO_DETECTION_YOLOv8-L)   |    512    |      31.6      |   169.8   |        91.2         |          62.9          |    10.95     |\r
| [RT-DETRv2-S](https://huggingface.co/jenhung/CNO_DETECTION_YOLOv8-L) |    512    |      20.0      |   60.0    |        87.6         |          39.6          |     5.51     |\r
| [RT-DETRv2-M](https://huggingface.co/jenhung/CNO_DETECTION_YOLOv8-L) |    512    |      31.0      |   100.0   |        84.0         |          37.2          |     7.48     |\r
| [RT-DETRv2-L](https://huggingface.co/jenhung/CNO_DETECTION_YOLOv8-L) |    512    |      42.0      |   136.0   |        84.3         |          33.4          |    13.50     |\r
| [RT-DETRv2-X](https://huggingface.co/jenhung/CNO_DETECTION_YOLOv8-L) |    512    |      76.0      |   259.0   |        83.3         |          32.0          |    21.15     |\r
\r
## **Dataset**\r
The corneocyte nanotexture dataset is available for download at the following link: [Corneocyte Nanotexture Dataset](https://huggingface.co/datasets/jenhung/Corneocyte_Nanotexture_Dataset).\r
\r
## **Contributions**\r
\r
[1] Liao, H-S., Wang, J-H., Raun, E., Nørgaard, L. O., Dons, F. E., & Hwu, E. E-T. (2022). Atopic Dermatitis Severity Assessment using High-Speed Dermal Atomic Force Microscope. Abstract from AFM BioMed Conference 2022, Nagoya-Okazaki, Japan.\r
\r
[2] Pereda, J., Liao, H-S., Werner, C., Wang, J-H., Huang, K-Y., Raun, E., Nørgaard, L. O., Dons, F. E., & Hwu, E. E. T. (2022). Hacking Consumer Electronics for Biomedical Imaging. Abstract from 5th Global Conference on Biomedical Engineering & Annual Meeting of TSBME, Taipei, Taiwan, Province of China.\r
\r
[3] Liao, H. S., Akhtar, I., Werner, C., Slipets, R., Pereda, J., Wang, J. H., Raun, E., Nørgaard, L. O., Dons, F. E., & Hwu, E. E. T. (2022). Open-source controller for low-cost and high-speed atomic force microscopy imaging of skin corneocyte nanotextures. HardwareX, 12, [e00341]. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ohx.2022.e00341\r
\r
----\r
\r
### Contact: [Jen-Hung Wang](mailto:jenhw@dtu.dk) / [Assoc. Professor En-Te Hwu](mailto:etehw@dtu.dk)\r
""" ;
