### **Using Dev Containers (Docker and VScode extension)**\r
\r
Most processes, such as Foldseek, use container ([BioContainers](https://quay.io/organization/biocontainers)), but some involve processing with jupyter notebook, which requires the preparation of some python libraries (e.g., polars.).\r
If you want to experiment with a simple workflow, you can create an analysis environment easily using [Dev Containers](https://github.com/yonesora56/plant2human/blob/main/.devcontainer/devcontainer.json) system, a VScode extension.\r
Using this environment, the version of the python library is probably the one used during development, so errors are unlikely to occur (see [Dockerfile](https://github.com/yonesora56/plant2human/blob/main/.devcontainer/Dockerfile) for the package version).\r
\r
Please check the official website for Dev Container details.\r
- [Developing inside a Container](https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/devcontainers/containers)\r
- [Development Containers](https://containers.dev/)\r
