git clone https://github.com/yonesora56/plant2human.git\r
cd ./plant2human/\r
```\r
\r
&nbsp;\r
\r
## 1. Creation of a TSV file of gene and UniProt ID correspondences ??\r
\r
First, you need the following [gene list tsv file](https://github.com/yonesora56/plant2human/blob/main/test/oryza_sativa_test_100genes_202603/oryza_sativa_random_100genes_list.tsv).\r
\r
**?? Note:** Please set the column name as "From"\r
\r
```tsv\r
From\r
Os12g0269700\r
Os10g0410900\r
Os05g0403000\r
Os06g0127250\r
Os02g0249600\r
Os09g0349700\r
Os03g0735150\r
Os08g0547350\r
Os06g0282400\r
Os05g0576750\r
Os07g0216600\r
Os10g0164500\r
Os07g0201300\r
Os01g0567200\r
Os05g0563050\r
Os03g0660050\r
Os11g0436450\r
...\r
```\r
\r
&nbsp;\r
\r
The following [TSV file](https://github.com/yonesora56/plant2human/blob/main/test/oryza_sativa_test_100genes_202603/os_100_genes_idmapping_all.tsv) is required to execute the following workflow.\r
\r
> **?? Note:** Network access required in this process!\r
\r
```tsv\r
From	UniProt Accession\r
Os01g0104800	A0A0N7KC66\r
Os01g0104800	Q657Z6\r
Os01g0104800	Q658C6\r
Os01g0152300	Q9LGI2\r
Os01g0322300	A0A9K3Y6N1\r
Os01g0322300	Q657N1\r
Os01g0567200	A0A0N7KD66\r
Os01g0567200	Q657K0\r
Os01g0571133	A0A0P0V4A8\r
Os01g0664500	A0A8J8XFG3\r
Os01g0664500	Q5SN58\r
Os01g0810800	A0A8J8XDQ1\r
Os01g0810800	B7FAC9\r
Os01g0875300	A0A0P0VB72\r
Os01g0924300	A0A0P0VCB7\r
...\r
```\r
\r
To do this, you need to follow the CWL workflow command below.\r
This YAML file is the parameter file for the workflow, for example.\r
\r
**?? Where to save:** Place your YAML file in the `job/` directory.\r
\r
&nbsp;\r
\r
## YAML Template for UniProt ID Mapping\r
\r
Below is a template YAML file for the UniProt ID mapping process.\r
Copy this template and modify the parameters marked with `# <-- CHANGE THIS!`.\r
\r
**Example file:** [`job/os_100genes_uniprot_idmapping.yml`](https://github.com/yonesora56/plant2human/blob/main/job/os_100genes_uniprot_idmapping.yml)\r
\r
```YAML\r
# ---------- OUTPUT SETTINGS ----------\r
# Output notebook filename (string)\r
output_notebook_name: "your_species_uniprot_idmapping.ipynb"  # <-- CHANGE THIS!\r
\r
# ---------- INPUT FILE ----------\r
# Your gene list TSV file (column header must be "From")\r
gene_id_file:\r
  class: File                                # <-- DO NOT CHANGE\r
  format: edam:format_3475  # <-- DO NOT CHANGE\r
  location: ./path/to/your_gene_list.tsv     # <-- CHANGE THIS! (path to your gene list)\r
\r
# ---------- UniProt API SETTINGS ----------\r
# For plant species, use "Ensembl_Genomes" as query database\r
uniprot_api_query_db: "Ensembl_Genomes"  # <-- DO NOT CHANGE (for plants)\r
uniprot_api_target_db: "UniProtKB"       # <-- DO NOT CHANGE\r
\r
# ---------- OUTPUT DIRECTORY/FILE NAMES ----------\r
# Directory for AlphaFold info JSON files\r
json_dir_name: "your_species_afinfo_json"           # <-- CHANGE THIS!\r
\r
# Structure file format: "cifUrl" for mmCIF file format (recommended), "pdbUrl" for PDB file format\r
data_url: "cifUrl"                                  # <-- Usually DO NOT CHANGE\r
\r
# Directory for downloaded structure files\r
structure_dir_name: "your_species_mmcif"            # <-- CHANGE THIS!\r
\r
# Output TSV filename for ID mapping results\r
id_mapping_all_file_name: "your_species_idmapping_all.tsv"  # <-- CHANGE THIS!\r
```\r
\r
&nbsp;\r
\r
&nbsp;\r
\r
&nbsp;\r
\r
