&nbsp;\r
\r
## rice vs human result (strngent mode result) ?? ↔ ??\r
\r
For example, you can visualize the results of structural similarity and global alignment, as shown below.\r
In this case, the x-axis represents the global alignment similarity match (%), and the y-axis represents the average lDDT score (an indicator of structural alignment).\r
\r
The hit pairs in the upper-right plot indicate higher sequence similarity and structural similarity.\r
\r
![image](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yonesora56/plant2human/main/test/oryza_sativa_test_100genes_202603/foldseek_result_similarity_percent_needle_lddt_all.png)\r
\r
&nbsp;\r
\r
In this case, the x-axis represents the local alignment similarity match (%), and the y-axis represents the average lDDT score (an indicator of structural alignment).\r
\r
![image](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yonesora56/plant2human/main/test/oryza_sativa_test_100genes_202603/foldseek_result_similarity_percent_water_lddt_all.png)\r
\r
&nbsp;\r
\r
&nbsp;\r
\r
## After Filtering\r
\r
The report notebook for the plant2human workflow also outputs scatter plots after applying the filtering conditions set in this workflow.\r
\r
## Filtering criteria\r
\r
1. structural alignment coverage >= 50%\r
2. If there are hits with the same target for the same gene-derived UniProt ID, the one with the highest qcov is selected, and if the qcov is the same, the one with the highest lDDT is selected.\r
\r
> **?? Note:** In this workflow, we leave the states with the same foldseek hit even if the query genes are different.\r
\r
3. Select hits that can be converted to Ensembl gene id and HGNC Gene nomenclature with [TogoID API](https://togoid.dbcls.jp/)\r
\r
&nbsp;\r
\r
By applying these filtering conditions, you can examine hit pairs that are easier to investigate!\r
\r
&nbsp;\r
\r
## Global alignment (x-axis) (After Filtering)\r
\r
![image](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yonesora56/plant2human/main/test/oryza_sativa_test_100genes_202603/foldseek_result_similarity_percent_needle_lddt_filter.png)\r
\r
&nbsp;\r
\r
## local alignment (x-axis) (After Filtering)\r
\r
![image](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yonesora56/plant2human/main/test/oryza_sativa_test_100genes_202603/foldseek_result_similarity_percent_water_lddt_filter.png)\r
\r
&nbsp;\r
