&nbsp;\r
\r
## ?? Running the Pipeline for Another Plant Species ??\r
\r
This workflow can be applied to **any plant species** available in the [AlphaFold Protein Structure Database (AFDB)](https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/).\r
\r
&nbsp;\r
\r
### Step 1: Check Species Availability in AFDB\r
\r
Before running the pipeline, verify that your target plant species is available:\r
\r
1. Visit [AFDB Page](https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/)\r
2. Search for your species name or UniProt proteome ID\r
3. Confirm protein structures are available for your genes\r
\r
**?? Note:** Most model organisms and many crop species are available in AFDB v6.\r
\r
&nbsp;\r
\r
### Step 2: Prepare Your Gene List\r
\r
Create a TSV file with column header "From" containing your gene IDs:\r
\r
| Species | Gene ID Format | Example |\r
|---------|----------------|---------|\r
| *Oryza sativa* | RAP-DB format | `Os01g0104800` |\r
| *Arabidopsis thaliana* | TAIR format | `AT1G01010` |\r
| *Zea mays* | Ensembl format | `Zm00001eb000010` |\r
| *Solanum lycopersicum* | Ensembl format | `Solyc01g005000` |\r
| *Glycine max* | Ensembl format | `Glyma.01G000100` |\r
\r
&nbsp;\r
\r
### Step 3: Create YAML Parameter Files\r
\r
1. **Copy the template** from [Section 1 (UniProt ID Mapping)](#yaml-template-for-uniprot-id-mapping) and [Section 3 (Main Workflow)](#yaml-template-for-stringent-mode)\r
2. **Modify the paths and filenames** marked with `# <-- CHANGE THIS!`\r
3. **Save your YAML files** in the `job/` directory\r
\r
&nbsp;\r
\r
### Step 4: Execute the Workflow\r
\r
Follow the same steps as described in Sections 1-3, using your custom YAML files.\r
\r
&nbsp;\r
\r
### ?? Example Implementations for Other Species\r
\r
We provide complete examples for multiple plant species. Use these as references:\r
\r
| Species | Test Directory | YAML Files |\r
|---------|----------------|------------|\r
| *Arabidopsis thaliana* | [`test/arabidopsis_test_100genes_202603/`](https://github.com/yonesora56/plant2human/blob/main/test/arabidopsis_test_100genes_202603/README.md) | [`job/at_100genes_*.yml`](https://github.com/yonesora56/plant2human/tree/main/job) |\r
| *Zea mays* | [`test/zea_mays_test_100genes_202603/`](https://github.com/yonesora56/plant2human/blob/main/test/zea_mays_test_100genes_202603/README.md) | [`job/zm_100genes_*.yml`](https://github.com/yonesora56/plant2human/tree/main/job) |\r
| *Solanum lycopersicum* | [`test/solanum_lycopersicum_test_100genes_202603/`](https://github.com/yonesora56/plant2human/blob/main/test/solanum_lycopersicum_test_100genes_202603/README.md) | [`job/sl_100genes_*.yml`](https://github.com/yonesora56/plant2human/tree/main/job) |\r
| *Glycine max* | [`test/glycine_max_test_100genes_202603/`](https://github.com/yonesora56/plant2human/blob/main/test/glycine_max_test_100genes_202603/README.md) | [`job/gm_100genes_*.yml`](https://github.com/yonesora56/plant2human/tree/main/job) |\r
\r
