<https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/1243?version=2> a ns1:ComputationalWorkflow ;
    dcterms:conformsTo "https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalWorkflow/1.0-RELEASE" ;
    ns1:citation "10.48546/workflowhub.workflow.1243.2" ;
    ns1:creator "Playbook Partnership NIH CFDE" ;
    ns1:dateCreated "2025-02-25" ;
    ns1:dateModified "2026-05-13" ;
    ns1:description """The workflow starts with selecting chr2:g.39417578C>G as the search term. The closest gene to the variant was found using MyVariant.info[1]. Gene expression in tumors for CDKL4 were queried from the Open Pediatric Cancer Atlas API[3]. Median expression of CDKL4 was obtained from the GTEx Portal[4] using the portal's API. To visualize the level of expression across tumor gene expression, a bar plot was created Fig.. \r
1. Lelong, S. et al. BioThings SDK: a toolkit for building high-performance data APIs in biomedical research. Bioinformatics vol. 38 2077–2079 (2022). doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btac017\r
3. Shapiro, J. A. et al. OpenPBTA: The Open Pediatric Brain Tumor Atlas. Cell Genomics vol. 3 100340 (2023). doi:10.1016/j.xgen.2023.100340\r
4. Lonsdale, J. et al. The Genotype-Tissue Expression (GTEx) project. Nature Genetics vol. 45 580–585 (2013). doi:10.1038/ng.2653""" ;
    ns1:identifier "1243" ;
    ns1:license "CC-BY-4.0" ;
    ns1:name "Use Case 7: Variant Expression in Tumor/Healthy" ;
    ns1:url <https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/1243?version=2> ;
