\r
  - A telomeric sequence, e.g., `TTAGGG`\r
\r
- `-entry`\r
  - ALL_FILES is the default and generates all accessory files as well as pretext maps\r
  - MAPS_ONLY generates only the pretext maps and static images\r
\r
Now, you can run the pipeline using:\r
\r
#### For ALL_FILES run\r
\r
```bash\r
nextflow run sanger-tol/curationpretext \\\r
  --input { input.fasta } \\\r
  --cram { path/to/cram/ } \\\r
  --reads { path/to/longread/fasta/ } \\\r
  --read_type { default is "hifi" }\r
  --sample { default is "pretext_rerun" } \\\r
  --teloseq { default is "TTAGGG" } \\\r
  --map_order { default is "unsorted" } \\\r
  --outdir { OUTDIR } \\\r
  -profile <docker/singularity/{institute}>\r
\r
```\r
\r
#### For MAPS_ONLY run\r
\r
```bash\r
nextflow run sanger-tol/curationpretext \\\r
  --input { input.fasta } \\\r
  --cram { path/to/cram/ } \\\r
  --reads { path/to/longread/fasta/ } \\\r
  --read_type { default is "hifi" }\r
  --sample { default is "pretext_rerun" } \\\r
  --teloseq { default is "TTAGGG" } \\\r
  --map_order { default is "unsorted" } \\\r
  --outdir { OUTDIR } \\\r
  -profile <docker/singularity/{institute}> \\\r
  -entry MAPS_ONLY \\\r
```\r
\r
> **Warning:**\r
> Please provide pipeline parameters via the CLI or Nextflow `-params-file` option. Custom config files including those\r
> provided by the `-c` Nextflow option can be used to provide any configuration _**except for parameters**_;\r
\r
For more details, please refer to the [usage documentation](https://pipelines.tol.sanger.ac.uk/curationpretext/usage) and the [parameter documentation](https://pipelines.tol.sanger.ac.uk/curationpretext/parameters).\r
\r
## Pipeline output\r
\r
To see the the results of a test run with a full size dataset refer to the [results](https://pipelines.tol.sanger.ac.uk/curationpretext/results) tab on the sanger-tol/curationpretext website pipeline page.\r
For more details about the output files and reports, please refer to the\r
[output documentation](https://pipelines.tol.sanger.ac.uk/curationpretext/output).\r
