<https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/1339?version=1> a ns1:ComputationalWorkflow ;
    dcterms:conformsTo "https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalWorkflow/1.0-RELEASE" ;
    ns1:citation "" ;
    ns1:creator "Raül Sirvent",
        "Rosa M Badia" ;
    ns1:dateCreated "2025-04-15" ;
    ns1:dateModified "2026-05-13" ;
    ns1:description """COMPSs Matrix Multiplication resourceUsage profiling example.\r
\r
MN5 MSIZE=20 BSIZE=768 7 Nodes (6 workers) (--num_nodes=7 --worker_in_master_cpus=0). \r
\r
* Total number of tasks: 20^3 = 8000\r
* Maximum code parallelism: 20^2 = 400\r
* Total cores: 112*6 = 672 \r
* Maximum utilisation: 400 / 112 = 3,57 Nodes\r
\r
Overall stats from "pycompss inspect":\r
\r
```\r
    │   └── overall\r
    │       ├── matmul_tasks\r
    │       │   └── multiply\r
    │       │       ├── maxTime = 91,111 ms\r
    │       │       ├── executions = 8,000 \r
    │       │       ├── avgTime = 84,839 ms\r
    │       │       └── minTime = 79,278 ms\r
    │       └── executionTime = 1,929,944 ms\r
```\r
\r
This example shows misuse of resources (from 6 workers, only 3 and a half can be exploited due to the application's inherent parallelism), which can be seen in the profiling folder plots.""" ;
