    ns1:description """# NGS Equimolar Pooling Calculator\r
\r
A web-based tool for calculating equimolar pooling volumes from complex sub-pools for Next-Generation Sequencing (NGS).\r
\r
## About\r
\r
This calculator helps researchers determine the correct volumes to take from each pool when combining multiple complex sub-pools of NGS libraries for sequencing. It ensures that each individual sample contributes an equal number of molecules to the final sequencing run, resulting in more balanced coverage.\r
\r
## Features\r
\r
- Calculate equimolar pooling volumes for any number of input pools\r
- Support for both calculated (estimated / target) and measured concentrations\r
- Option to maximize the usage of original pools\r
- Adjustable final volume\r
- Real-time results with detailed metrics\r
- Verification of equimolarity across samples\r
\r
## Live Calculator\r
\r
The calculator is available at: https://bwprice.github.io/ngs-equimolar-pooling-calculator/\r
\r
## Usage\r
\r
1. Enter information for each input pool:\r
   - Molarity that each sample was normalized to in the sub-pool - i.e. the target molarity when pooling (nM)\r
   - Total pool volume (μl)\r
   - Number of samples in the pool\r
   - (Optional) Measured concentration of each sub-pool from lab quantification\r
\r
2. Choose whether to:\r
   - Use measured concentrations (if available from Qubit, Bioanalyzer, qPCR, etc.)\r
   - Maximize usage of original pools\r
   - Set a specific final pool volume\r
\r
3. The calculator will automatically determine:\r
   - How much volume to take from each sub-pool\r
   - The percentage of each sub-pool that will be used\r
   - The final nM contribution per sample\r
   - Total samples in the final pool\r
\r
## Installation for Local Development\r
\r
1. Clone this repository:\r
   ```\r
   git clone https://github.com/bwprice/ngs-equimolar-pooling-calculator.git\r
   cd ngs-equimolar-pooling-calculator\r
   ```\r
\r
2. Install dependencies:\r
   ```\r
   npm install\r
   ```\r
\r
3. Start the development server:\r
   ```\r
   npm start\r
   ```\r
\r
4. Open [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000) to view it in your browser.\r
\r
## Deployment\r
\r
To deploy to GitHub Pages:\r
\r
```\r
npm run deploy\r
```\r
\r
## Contributing\r
\r
Contributions are welcome! Please feel free to submit a Pull Request.\r
\r
## License\r
\r
This project is licensed under the MIT License - see the LICENSE file for details.\r
\r
## Citation\r
\r
If you use this tool in your research, please cite:\r
\r
```\r
Ben Price, NGS Equimolar Pooling Calculator, GitHub Repository, 2025, \r
Available at: https://github.com/bwprice/ngs-equimolar-pooling-calculator\r
```\r
""" ;
    ns1:identifier "1344" ;
