<https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/1748?version=1> a ns1:ComputationalWorkflow ;
    dcterms:conformsTo "https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalWorkflow/1.0-RELEASE" ;
    ns1:citation "" ;
    ns1:dateCreated "2025-06-24" ;
    ns1:dateModified "2026-09-14" ;
    ns1:description """Image processing from movies to micrographs, including CTF estimation and quality filters for image curation.\r
Scipion required plugins: pwem, motioncorr, cistem, emfacilities\r
\r
\r
**Adapting to Tilted Samples**\r
\r
To process tilted experiments, use ”tilted” templates. These are modified workflows tailored to handle high drift and lower resolution commonly observed in tilted samples. Key adjustments include:\r
\r
* **Motion Correction Filters**: Max per-frame shift = 30; Global drift = 120.\r
\r
\r
* **CTF Consensus Filters**: Adapted to 6.5 Å and 8.5 Å resolution cutoffs.\r
\r
\r
* **Defocus Sampler**: Trains with 500 images to select 25 diverse examples, ensuring a generalizable picking model.\r
""" ;
    ns1:identifier "1748" ;
    ns1:license "CC-BY-4.0" ;
    ns1:name "Workflow simple processing (tilted experiments variation)" ;
    ns1:url <https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/1748?version=1> ;
    ns1:version "1" .

