<https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/1782?version=3> a ns1:ComputationalWorkflow ;
    dcterms:conformsTo "https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalWorkflow/1.0-RELEASE" ;
    ns1:citation "10.48546/workflowhub.workflow.1782.3" ;
    ns1:creator "Bradley Pease",
        "Cameron Hyde",
        "Grace Sun",
        "Lanxi (Daisy) Li",
        "Magdalena Antczak",
        "Michael Thang",
        "Sarah Williams",
        "Shaun Bochow",
        "Valentine Murigneux" ;
    ns1:dateCreated "2025-07-08" ;
    ns1:dateModified "2026-05-13" ;
    ns1:description """<table>\r
  <tr>\r
    <td style="vertical-align:top; width:50%;">\r
      <img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcif/taxodactyl/main/docs/images/taxodactyl_logo.png" alt="taxodactyl-logo" width="100%"/>\r
    </td>\r
    <td style="vertical-align:top; width:50%;">\r
      <strong>qcif/taxodactyl</strong> is a modular, reproducible Nextflow workflow for the conservative taxonomy assignment to DNA sequences, designed for high-confidence, auditable results in biosecurity and biodiversity contexts. The workflow integrates multiple bioinformatics tools and databases, automates best-practice analysis steps, and produces detailed reports with supporting evidence for each taxonomic assignment.\r
    </td>\r
  </tr>\r
</table>\r
\r
<p align="center" style="max-width:400px; margin:auto;">\r
    <img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcif/taxodactyl/main/docs/images/taxodactyl_diagram.png" alt="taxodactyl_diagram" width="350"/>\r
</p>\r
\r
### Workflow Overview\r
\r
The pipeline orchestrates a series of analytical steps, each encapsulated in a dedicated module or subworkflow. The main stages are:\r
\r
1. **Environment Configuration** Sets up environment variables and paths required for downstream processes, ensuring reproducibility and portability.\r
\r
2. **Input Validation** Checks the integrity and compatibility of input files (FASTA sequences, metadata, databases), preventing downstream errors.\r
\r
3. **Sequence Search**  \r
   - **[BLAST Core Nucleotide Database](https://ncbiinsights.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2024/07/18/new-blast-core-nucleotide-database/) ([BLASTN](https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi)):** Queries input sequences against the NCBI nucleotide database using BLASTN.\r
   - **[BOLD v4](https://v4.boldsystems.org/) ([API](https://v4.boldsystems.org/index.php/api_home)):** Queries input sequences against the Barcode of Life Data Systems. Taxonomic lineage included in the results.\r
\r
4. **Hit Extraction** Parses BLAST results to extract relevant hits for each query.\r
\r
5. **Taxonomic ID Extraction** Retrieves taxonomic IDs for BLAST hits.\r
\r
6. **Taxonomic Lineage Extraction** Maps taxonomic IDs to full lineages, enabling downstream filtering and reporting.\r
\r
7. **Candidate Extraction** Identifies candidate species for each query, applying user-defined thresholds for identity and coverage.\r
\r
8. **Supporting Evidence Evaluation**  \r
   - **Publications Diversity:** Assesses the diversity of data sources supporting each candidate.\r
   - **Database Coverage:** Evaluates the representation of candidates in global databases ([GBIF](https://www.gbif.org/), [GenBank](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/genbank/), [BOLD](https://v4.boldsystems.org/)).\r
\r
9. **Multiple Sequence Alignment ([MAFFT](https://mafft.cbrc.jp/alignment/server/index.html))** Aligns candidate and query sequences to prepare for phylogenetic analysis.\r
\r
10. **Phylogenetic Tree Construction ([FastMe](http://www.atgc-montpellier.fr/fastme/))** Builds a phylogenetic tree to visualise relationships among candidates and queries.\r
\r
11. **Comprehensive Reporting** Generates detailed HTML and text reports, including sequence alignments, phylogenetic trees, database coverage, and all supporting evidence for each assignment.\r
""" ;
    ns1:identifier "1782" ;
    ns1:license "MIT" ;
    ns1:name "TAXODACTYL - High-confidence, evidence-based taxonomic assignment of DNA sequences" ;
    ns1:url <https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/1782?version=3> ;
    ns1:version "3" .

<https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/1784?version=1> a ns1:ComputationalWorkflow ;
    dcterms:conformsTo "https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalWorkflow/1.0-RELEASE" ;
    ns1:applicationSubCategory <http://edamontology.org/topic_0196>,
