\r
## Introduction\r
\r
**EarlhamInst/eisca** is a bioinformatics pipeline that performs analysis for single-cell RNA-seq data. The pipeline is built using [Nextflow](https://www.nextflow.io/). The pipeline was developed as a generalized, flexible, and scalable workflow for scRNA-seq analysis. It is primarily designed for droplet-based (10x) and plate-based (Smart-seq2) data. The pipeline can be applied from multiple starting points, either from raw FASTQ data or single-cell AnnData for the specified analysis phase.\r
\r
\r
The modules of the pipeline are listed as follows:\r
- **Primary analysis**\r
  - FastQC - Raw read QC\r
  - TrimGalore - Adapter and quality trimming to FastQ files\r
  - Kallisto & Bustools - Mapping & quantification by Kallisto & Bustools\r
  - Salmon Alevin - Mapping & quantification by Salmon Alevin\r
  - STARsolo - Mapping & quantification by STAR\r
  - MTX conversion - Converting count matrixes into Anndata objects\r
  - CONCAT counts - Concatenating input Anndata objects into one Anndata object\r
- **Secondary analysis**\r
  - QC & cell filtering - cell filtering and QC on raw data and filtered data\r
  - Clustering analysis - single-cell clustering analysis\r
  - Merging/integration of samples \r
- **Tertiary analysis**\r
  - Cell type annotation\r
  - Differential expression analysis\r
  - Cell-cell communication analysis\r
  - Trajectory & pseudotime analysis (to be implemented)\r
  - Other downstream analyses (to be implemented)\r
- **Pipeline reporting**\r
  - Analysis report - Single-ell Analysis Report.\r
  - MultiQC - Aggregate report describing results and QC for tools registered in nf-core\r
  - Pipeline information - Report metrics generated during the workflow execution\r
\r
\r
