    ns1:description """MAGNETO is an automated snakemake workflow dedicated to MAG (Metagenome-Assembled Genomes) reconstruction from metagenomic data. \r
\r
It includes a fully-automated coassembly step informed by optimal clustering of metagenomic distances, and implements complementary genome binning strategies, for improving MAG recovery.\r
\r
# Key Features\r
\r
 - **Quality Control (QC)**: Automatically assesses the quality and the contamination of input reads, ensuring that low-quality data are filtered out to improve downstream analyses.\r
\r
 - **Assembly**: MAGNETO uses high-performance assembler to construct contigs from metagenomic reads.\r
\r
 - **Gene Collection**: Extracts and compiles gene sequences from contigs, providing a comprehensive gene catalog directly after assembly.\r
\r
 - **Binning**: Groups contigs into probable genomes using composition signatures and abundance profiles.\r
\r
 - **Genomes collection**: Provides taxonomic and functional annotation of reconstructed MAGs.\r
\r
 - **Metatranscriptomic mapping**: Mapping of transcriptomic reads on genes collection and/or MAGs obtained with previous analysis.\r
\r
# Documentation\r
\r
**Full description in the [wiki pages](https://gitlab.univ-nantes.fr/bird_pipeline_registry/magneto/-/wikis/home)**\r
\r
# Citing the pipeline \r
Churcheward B, Millet M, Bihouée A, Fertin G, Chaffron S.<br>\r
MAGNETO: An Automated Workflow for Genome-Resolved Metagenomics.<br>\r
mSystems. 2022 Jun 15:e0043222. doi: [10.1128/msystems.00432-22](https://doi.org/10.1128/msystems.00432-22)\r
""" ;
