<https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/1841?version=1> a ns1:ComputationalWorkflow ;
    dcterms:conformsTo "https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalWorkflow/1.0-RELEASE" ;
    ns1:citation "" ;
    ns1:creator "Tong LI" ;
    ns1:dateCreated "2025-07-29" ;
    ns1:dateModified "2025-07-29" ;
    ns1:description """PaSTa is a nextflow-based end-to-end image analysis pipeline for decoding image-based spatial transcriptomics data. It performs imaging cycle registration, cell segmentation and transcripts peak decoding. It is currently supports analysis of three types of ST technology:\r
\r
- in-situ sequencing-like encoding\r
- MERFISH-like encoding\r
- RNAScope-like labelling\r
\r
Prerequisites:\r
1. Nextflow. Installation guide: https://www.nextflow.io/docs/latest/getstarted.html\r
2. Docker or Singularity. Installation guide: https://docs.docker.com/get-docker/ or https://sylabs.io/guides/3.7/user-guide/quick_start.html\r
\r
Demo run with GitPod\r
1. Clone the repository\r
```\r
git clone https://github.com/cellgeni/Image-ST.git\r
```\r
2. Prepare the run.config file *\r
```\r
process {\r
        withName: CELLPOSE {\r
                ext.args = "--channels [0,0]"\r
                storeDir = "./output/naive_cellpose_segmentation/"\r
        }\r
\r
        withName: POSTCODE {\r
                memory = {20.Gb * task.attempt}\r
                storeDir = "./output/PoSTcode_decoding_output"\r
        }\r
\r
        withName: TO_SPATIALDATA {\r
                memory = {20.Gb * task.attempt}\r
                ext.args = "--feature_col 'Name' --expansion_in_pixels 30 --save_label_img False"\r
        }\r
\r
        withName: MERGE_OUTLINES {\r
                storeDir = "./output/merged_cellpose_segmentation/"\r
        }\r
\r
        withName: BIOINFOTONGLI_MICROALIGNER {\r
                memory = {50.Gb * task.attempt}\r
                storeDir = "./output/registered_stacks"\r
        }\r
\r
        withName: BIOINFOTONGLI_TILEDSPOTIFLOW {\r
                memory = {30.Gb * task.attempt}\r
                storeDir = "./output/spotiflow_peaks/"\r
        }\r
\r
        withName: BIOINFOTONGLI_MERGEPEAKS {\r
                memory = {50.Gb * task.attempt}\r
                storeDir = "./output/spotiflow_peaks/"\r
        }\r
\r
        withName: BIOINFOTONGLI_CONCATENATEWKTS {\r
                memory = {50.Gb * task.attempt}\r
                storeDir = "./output/spotiflow_peaks/"\r
        }\r
\r
        withName: EXTRACT_PEAK_PROFILE {\r
                memory = {50.Gb * task.attempt}\r
                storeDir = "./output/peak_profiles/"\r
        }\r
}\r
```\r
3. Prepare the parameters file (e.g. iss.yaml)\r
```\r
images:\r
   - ['id': "test",\r
       [\r
         "cycle1.ome.tiff",\r
         "cycle2.ome.tiff",\r
         "cycle3.ome.tiff",\r
         "cycle4.ome.tiff",\r
         "cycle5.ome.tiff",\r
         "cycle6.ome.tiff",\r
       ]\r
     ]\r
cell_diameters: [30]\r
chs_to_call_peaks: [1,2] // channels to call peaks, can be multiple\r
codebook:\r
  - ['id': "test", "./codebook.csv", "./dummy.txt"] // has to match the meta in `images` variable\r
segmentation_method: "CELLPOSE" // or DEEPCELL or STARDIST or INSTANSEG\r
\r
out_dir: "./output"\r
```\r
4. Run the pipeline\r
```\r
nextflow run ./Image-ST/main.nf -profile lsf,singularity -c run.config -params-file iss.yaml -entry RUN_DECODING -resume\r
```\r
5. Check the output in the specified storeDir.\r
\r
Spin up Napari with napari-spatialdata plugin installed (https://spatialdata.scverse.org/projects/napari/en/latest/notebooks/spatialdata.html)\r
\r
Then use the following command to visualize the output\r
```\r
from napari_spatialdata import Interactive\r
import spatialdata as spd\r
\r
data = spd.read_zarr([path-to-.sdata-folder])\r
Interactive(data)\r
```\r
\r
*: You may leave the process block empty if you want to use the default parameters.\r
\r
FAQ\r
---\r
\r
1. My HOME dir is full when running Singularity image conversion on HPC.\r
\r
A quick solution is to manually specify singularity dir by setting:\r
\r
\r
```\r
singularity cache clean\r
export SINGULARITY_CACHEDIR=./singularity_image_dir\r
export NXF_SINGULARITY_CACHEDIR=./singularity_image_dir\r
```\r
\r
2. How do I modify parameters to specific process/step?\r
\r
By following nf-core standard, it is possible to add any parameters to the main script using ext.args=”--[key] [value]” in the run.config file.\r
\r
An example is\r
\r
withName: POSTCODE {\r
    ext.args = "--codebook_targer_col L-probe --codebook_code_col code "\r
}\r
\r
3. Cannot download pretrained model for the deep-learning tools (Spotiflow/CellPose)\r
\r
> Exception: URL fetch failure on https://drive.switch.ch/index.php/s/6AoTEgpIAeQMRvX/download: None -- [Errno -3] Temporary failure in name resolution\r
Or CellPose\r
urllib.error.URLError: <urlopen error [Errno -3] Temporary failure in name resolution>\r
\r
Mostly likely you've reached max download (?), wait a bit and try later OR manually download those models and update the configuration file.""" ;
