<https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/1858?version=1> a ns1:ComputationalWorkflow ;
    dcterms:conformsTo "https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalWorkflow/1.0-RELEASE" ;
    ns1:citation "10.48546/workflowhub.workflow.1858.1" ;
    ns1:creator "Zhixing Feng" ;
    ns1:dateCreated "2025-08-12" ;
    ns1:dateModified "2025-08-20" ;
    ns1:description """# NanoFreeLunch\r
\r
Detecting DNA modifications quantitatively from Nanopore data without using raw signals.\r
\r
# Installation\r
\r
1. Install Julia from https://julialang.org/. Do Not use Julia in containers like docker or singularity. \r
2. Enter the folder of NanoFreeLunch and type `julia setup.jl`.\r
3. The executable can be found in build/bin/, add the folder to PATH or add softlink of the executable to the folder in your PATH.\r
\r
**Warning**: you might experience slow package downloading or get error like `Exception: RequestError: HTTP/1.1 200 Connection established ` if Julia server connection is unstable in your region. You could change your Julia server by typing `export JULIA_PKG_SERVER=https://mirrors.pku.edu.cn/julia` and try again. Here is a list of alternative Julia package servers: \r
```\r
https://mirrors.pku.edu.cn/julia\r
https://mirrors.sjtug.sjtu.edu.cn/julia\r
https://mirrors.nju.edu.cn/julia\r
https://releases.tongyuan.cc/juliapkg/original\r
```\r
\r
# Demo \r
A quick demo is available at https://gitee.com/zhixingfeng/nfl-demo/tree/main/demo.\r
\r
# Supporting data and code\r
The supporting data and code to reproduce the results are available at https://gitee.com/zhixingfeng/nfl-demo. \r
\r
# Usage \r
## Extracting features from aligned reads\r
\r
### `prepdata [options] [flags] bamfile reffile locifile outdir`\r
\r
### Args\r
\r
- `<modelfile>`  \r
  The model file, which is the output file of `nfl train`.\r
\r
- `<Xdata_dir>`  \r
  The `Xdata` folder in the output directory of `nfl prepdata`.\r
\r
- `<outfile>`  \r
  The output file (predicted modification level for qualitative detection or probability for qualitative detection).\r
\r
### Options\r
\r
- `-e`, `--esp <0.001>`  \r
  Precision threshold. Modification level <= `esp` will be set to 0, and modification level >= `1-esp` will be set to 1.\r
\r
- `-s`, `--subset <"">`  \r
  Use a subset of features (default: using all the features).\r
\r
- `--objective <reg:squarederror>`  \r
  Default is `reg:squarederror`. Use `reg:logistic` for direct regression instead of logit transformation.\r
\r
### Flags\r
\r
- `-h`, `--help`  \r
  Print this help message.\r
\r
\r
# License\r
The software is under GPL3 and the data in `test/data` and `test/results` are under the CC0 public domain waiver. \r
\r
\r
""" ;
