<https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/1960?version=1> a ns1:ComputationalWorkflow ;
    dcterms:conformsTo "https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalWorkflow/1.0-RELEASE" ;
    ns1:applicationSubCategory <http://edamontology.org/topic_0091>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_0196>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3174> ;
    ns1:citation "10.48546/workflowhub.workflow.1960.1" ;
    ns1:creator "Caner Bagci" ;
    ns1:dateCreated "2025-09-19" ;
    ns1:dateModified "2025-09-19" ;
    ns1:description """# Soil Metagenome Pipeline\r
\r
Soil Metagenome Pipeline is a modular, Nextflow DSL2 workflow for assembling, polishing, binning, annotating, and functionally characterizing complex soil metagenomes. It orchestrates state-of-the-art tools for long- and short-read metagenomics, generates high-quality MAGs, assigns taxonomy, and screens for biosynthetic gene clusters (BGCs).\r
\r
## What it does\r
- Assembles long-read metagenomes (e.g., ONT) with Flye and optionally polishes with Medaka and/or NextPolish using short reads.\r
- Maps short/long reads to assemblies to compute coverage/depth for downstream binning and QC.\r
- Bins contigs with multiple strategies (SemiBin2, VAMB, MetaCoAG, ComeBIN) and can integrate results.\r
- Evaluates MAG quality with CheckM2 and assigns taxonomy with GTDB-Tk.\r
- Annotates bins and/or assemblies (Bakta, eggNOG) and detects BGCs (antiSMASH) with network-based clustering (BiG-SCAPE).\r
- Produces organized outputs suitable for downstream comparative genomics.\r
\r
## Key features\r
- Modular DSL2 design: swap/extend modules under `modules/` and `submodules/`.\r
- Reproducible runtime via Conda/containers (profiles in `conf/`).\r
- Sensible defaults with overridable parameters via `nextflow.config` or CLI.\r
- Caching and resumability: supports `-resume` for efficient re-runs.\r
\r
## Modules at a glance (non-exhaustive)\r
- Assembly and polishing: Flye, Medaka, NextPolish\r
- Coverage mapping: minimap2/samtools, coverm, strobealign\r
- Binning: SemiBin2, VAMB, MetaCoAG, ComeBIN, plus bin collection utilities\r
- QC and taxonomy: CheckM2, GTDB-Tk\r
- Annotation and function: Bakta (assemblies/bins), eggNOG\r
- BGC discovery: antiSMASH (assemblies/bins), BiG-SCAPE networks\r
- Taxonomic profiling: MMseqs2/MetaBuli helpers\r
\r
## Inputs\r
- Reads: long reads (ONT/PacBio), optional short reads (Illumina).\r
- Sample sheet: a tab-separated file like `data/samples.tsv` describing sample IDs and file paths.\r
- Reference databases: external DBs required by some tools (e.g., GTDB-Tk, antiSMASH, BiG-SCAPE) are not bundled. Configure their locations via params or environment as appropriate.\r
\r
## Quick start\r
- Dry run / graph preview:\r
  nextflow run . -dsl2 -preview\r
\r
- Example execution (adjust paths and profile to your environment):\r
  nextflow run . -profile conda -resume \\\r
    --reads '/path/to/*_{R1,R2}.fastq.gz' \\\r
    --longreads '/path/to/*.fastq.gz' \\\r
    --samples 'data/samples.tsv' \\\r
    --outdir 'results'\r
\r
See `conf/` for example profiles (conda, docker, singularity, slurm). Tune resources via `nextflow.config` using `withName:` blocks for process-specific CPU, memory, and time.\r
\r
## Citation\r
If you use Soil Metagenome Pipeline in your research, please cite the corresponding preprint:\r
\r
- bioRxiv abstract: https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/2025.05.28.656579v1.abstract\r
- DOI: https://doi.org/10.1101/2025.05.28.656579\r
\r
A machine-readable citation file (CITATION.cff) is included in the repository root. GitHub will display a "Cite this repository" button.\r
\r
## License\r
This project is licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later). See the LICENSE file for the full text.\r
""" ;
