    ns1:dateModified "2025-09-26" ;
    ns1:description """This project is an analysis pipeline using **Snakemake** for RNAseq analysis in order to find differentially expressed genes.\r
It has been widely tested on human RNA sequencing from an Illumina HiSeq but should work on most systems and many other species, provided the necessary resource files can be downloaded.  \r
\r
### Description\r
\r
**This pipeline is set for paired-end data only from Illumina HiSeq output files.**\r
\r
The main steps of the pipeline are:\r
\r
- optionnal cleaning data with [prinseq](http://prinseq.sourceforge.net/) and/or [cutadapt](http://cutadapt.readthedocs.io/en/stable/guide.html)\r
- alignment of reads on reference genome with [STAR](https://github.com/alexdobin/STAR)\r
- counting features with [HTSeq](http://htseq.readthedocs.io/)\r
- detection of DGE genes with [DESeq2](https://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/DESeq2.html)\r
- functional annotations with [ClusterProfiler](http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/clusterProfiler.html) on GO and KEGG databases\r
""" ;
