    ns1:description """# AnnoOddities\r
\r
AnnoOddies is a Python utility for detecting, identifying and characterising oddities in genome annotations. It parses and integrates statistics from multiple tools - including [AGAT](https://github.com/NBISweden/AGAT), [Mikado](https://github.com/EI-CoreBioinformatics/mikado), and [GFFread](https://github.com/gpertea/gffread), to generate a harmonised set of extended metrics that help assess annotation quality and highlight potential anomalies within genome annotations.\r
\r
In addition to summarising standard outputs, AnnoOddities computes a range of additional “oddity” measures, for example, counts of unusually large or small introns, exons, and untranslated regions; detection of transcripts lacking start or stop codons; identification of in-frame stop codons; estimation of canonical intron proportions; and more. These metrics help flag potential structural inconsistencies or systematic issues in gene models. The consolidated outputs include both summary statistics and detailed per-transcript results, exported in widely used machine- and human-readable formats (TSV, CSV, JSON, YAML, TOML) for flexible downstream analysis and visualisation.\r
\r
Currently, AnnoOddities runs [AGAT](https://github.com/NBISweden/AGAT), [Mikado](https://github.com/EI-CoreBioinformatics/mikado), and [GFFread](https://github.com/gpertea/gffread) to generate and combine statistics into unified reports. Future developments will focus on extending the workflow to incorporate additional quality assessment tools such as BUSCO and OMArk, enabling integrated comparisons of annotation and genome completeness metrics.\r
\r
This tool was developed as part of **[BioHackathon 2025](https://biohackathon-europe.org/), Project 23: Streamlining FAIR Metadata for Biodiversity Genome Annotations**.\r
Project details: https://github.com/elixir-europe/biohackathon-projects-2025/blob/main/23.md\r
\r
\r
## Installation\r
\r
All installation methods below will install AnnoOddities along with its dependencies.\r
\r
### Docker Installation\r
AnnoOddities can be installed with Docker. If you don't have Docker, please install [docker](https://docs.docker.com/get-docker/) first. Then you can pull the Docker image with AnnoOddities installed\r
\r
```console\r
VERSION=0.1.0\r
docker run gemygk/annooddities:v${VERSION} annooddities -h\r
```\r
\r
### Singularity Installation\r
AnnoOddities can be installed with Singularity. If you don't have Singularity, please install [singularity](https://docs.sylabs.io/guides/3.9/user-guide/quick_start.html#quick-installation-steps) first. Then you can pull the singularity image with AnnoOddities installed.\r
\r
We can directly run AnnoOddities from the Singularity image hosted on DockerHub\r
```console\r
VERSION=0.1.0\r
singularity exec docker://gemygk/annooddities:v${VERSION} annooddities -h\r
```\r
\r
Or, we can build and run a Singularity image, following the steps below:\r
```console\r
# Create a Singularity definition file, like below:\r
\r
$ cat annooddities-0.1.0.def\r
bootstrap: docker\r
from: gemygk/annooddities:v0.1.0\r
\r
# Build the Singularity image\r
$ sudo singularity build annooddities-0.1.0.sif annooddities-0.1.0.def\r
\r
# Execute AnnoOddities from the Singularity image\r
$ singularity exec annooddities-0.1.0.sif annooddities -h\r
```\r
\r
### Usage\r
```console\r
$ annooddities -h\r
usage: annooddities.py [-h] --genome_fasta GENOME_FASTA --gff3_file GFF3_FILE [--five_prime_utr_length FIVE_PRIME_UTR_LENGTH] [--three_prime_utr_length THREE_PRIME_UTR_LENGTH] [--five_utr_num FIVE_UTR_NUM] [--three_utr_num THREE_UTR_NUM]\r
                        [--min_intron_length MIN_INTRON_LENGTH] [--max_intron_length MAX_INTRON_LENGTH] [--min_exon_length MIN_EXON_LENGTH] [--max_exon_length MAX_EXON_LENGTH] [--selected_cds_fraction SELECTED_CDS_FRACTION]\r
                        [--canonical_intron_motifs CANONICAL_INTRON_MOTIFS] [--output_prefix OUTPUT_PREFIX] [--force] [--verbosity {debug,info,warning,error,critical}]\r
\r
Find annotation oddities from GFF3 and genome FASTA files\r
\r
optional arguments:\r
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\r
  --genome_fasta GENOME_FASTA\r
                        Provide Genome FASTA file\r
  --gff3_file GFF3_FILE\r
                        Provide GFF3 file with transcript annotations\r
  --output_prefix OUTPUT_PREFIX\r
                        Provide sample prefix for the output table [default:output]\r
  --force               Force rerun even if output files exist\r
  --verbosity {debug,info,warning,error,critical}\r
                        Set logging verbosity level [default:info]\r
\r
Oddity Thresholds:\r
  --five_prime_utr_length FIVE_PRIME_UTR_LENGTH\r
                        Threshold for 5' UTR length oddity [default:10000]\r
  --three_prime_utr_length THREE_PRIME_UTR_LENGTH\r
                        Threshold for 3' UTR length oddity [default:10000]\r
  --five_utr_num FIVE_UTR_NUM\r
                        Threshold for 5' UTR exon number oddity [default:5]\r
  --three_utr_num THREE_UTR_NUM\r
                        Threshold for 3' UTR exon number oddity [default:4]\r
  --min_intron_length MIN_INTRON_LENGTH\r
                        Threshold for minimum intron length oddity [default:5]\r
  --max_intron_length MAX_INTRON_LENGTH\r
                        Threshold for maximum intron length oddity.\r
                        Below are some guidelines:\r
                        - For fungi species, consider setting this to 1000 bp.\r
                        - For plant species, consider setting this to 10000 bp.\r
                        - For invertebrates species, consider setting this to 60000 bp.\r
                        - For vertebrates species, consider setting this to 120000 bp.\r
                        [default:120000]\r
  --min_exon_length MIN_EXON_LENGTH\r
                        Threshold for minimum exon length oddity [default:5]\r
  --max_exon_length MAX_EXON_LENGTH\r
                        Threshold for maximum exon length oddity [default:10000]\r
  --selected_cds_fraction SELECTED_CDS_FRACTION\r
                        Threshold for selected CDS fraction oddity.\r
                        This is the proportion of coding sequence to that of the transcript.\r
                        Values range from 0.0 to 1.0 [default:0.3]\r
  --canonical_intron_motifs CANONICAL_INTRON_MOTIFS\r
                        Comma-separated list of canonical intron motifs. [default:'GT-AG,GC-AG,AT-AC']\r
```\r
\r
## Running AnnoOddities\r
\r
### Example Command\r
To run AnnoOddities, use the command line interface with the required arguments for the genome FASTA file and GFF3 annotation file. For example:\r
```console\r
annooddities \\\r
    --genome_fasta input_genome.fna \\\r
    --gff3_file input_genome.gff\r
```\r
\r
You can also specify optional parameters to customise the oddity detection thresholds. For example, to set custom thresholds for minimum exon length and maximum intron length (for plants), you can run:\r
```console\r
annooddities \\\r
    --genome_fasta input_genome.fna \\\r
    --gff3_file input_genome.gff \\\r
    --min_exon_length 3 \\\r
    --max_intron_length 10000\r
```\r
\r
Or, if you want to restrict canonical intron motifs to only 'GT-AG', you can run:\r
```console\r
annooddities \\\r
    --genome_fasta input_genome.fna \\\r
    --gff3_file input_genome.gff \\\r
    --canonical_intron_motifs 'GT-AG'\r
```\r
\r
## Output\r
\r
An example output directory structure:\r
```console\r
CMD: annooddities --genome_fasta input_genome.fna --gff3_file input_genome.gff\r
\r
DIRECTORY: output_directory\r
├── input_genome.fna\r
├── input_genome.gff\r
├── input_genome.agat.log\r
├── output.agat_standardised.gff\r
├── output.agat_standardised.log\r
├── output.agat_standardised.agat.log\r
├── output.agat_sp_statistics.yaml\r
├── output.agat_sp_statistics.txt\r
├── output.agat_sp_statistics.log\r
├── output.agat_sp_statistics.json\r
├── output.agat_sp_statistics.toml\r
├── input_genome.fna.fai\r
├── output.gffread_table.log\r
├── output.gffread_table.tbl\r
├── output.mikado_tab_stats.log\r
├── output.mikado_tab_stats.tsv\r
├── output.mikado_stats.tsv\r
├── output.mikado_stats.yaml\r
├── output.mikado_summary_stats.tsv\r
├── output.mikado_stats.json\r
├── output.mikado_stats.toml\r
├── oddity_files\r
│   ├── output.AnnoOddities.has_inframe_stop.gff\r
│   ├── output.AnnoOddities.max_exon_length_gt_10000.gff\r
│   ├── output.AnnoOddities.min_exon_length_lte_5.gff\r
│   ├── output.AnnoOddities.exon_num_eq_1.gff\r
│   ├── output.AnnoOddities.exon_num_gt_1.gff\r
│   ├── output.AnnoOddities.is_fragment.gff\r
│   ├── output.AnnoOddities.not_has_start_codon.gff\r
│   ├── output.AnnoOddities.not_has_stop_codon.gff\r
│   ├── output.AnnoOddities.not_is_complete.gff\r
│   └── output.AnnoOddities.selected_cds_fraction_lte_0.3.gff\r
├── output.AnnoOddities.combined_statistics.yaml\r
├── output.AnnoOddities.combined_statistics.json\r
├── output.AnnoOddities.combined_statistics.toml\r
├── output.AnnoOddities.all_stats.tsv\r
├── output.AnnoOddities.gff\r
└── output.AnnoOddities.oddity_summary.txt\r
\r
```\r
\r
### AnnoOddities Summary\r
Provides both high-level summaries and more granular diagnostic reports to support manual review or automated pipelines.\r
\r
Below is an example of the `AnnoOddities.oddity_summary.txt` output file:\r
```console\r
FILE: output.AnnoOddities.oddity_summary.txt\r
AnnoOddities                      output\r
exon_num == 1                     4520\r
exon_num > 1                      12900\r
five_utr_length > 10000           0\r
five_utr_num > 5                  0\r
three_utr_length > 10000          0\r
three_utr_num > 4                 0\r
not is_complete                   428\r
not has_start_codon               174\r
not has_stop_codon                280\r
is_fragment                       26\r
has_inframe_stop                  1\r
max_exon_length > 10000           8\r
max_intron_length > 120000        0\r
min_exon_length <= 5              308\r
0 < min_intron_length <= 5        0\r
selected_cds_fraction <= 0.3      158\r
canonical_intron_proportion != 1  0\r
only_non_canonical_splicing       0\r
suspicious_splicing               0\r
```\r
\r
### AnnoOddities All Stats\r
Detailed per-transcript statistics (as detailed below) computed by AnnoOddities.\r
\r
Below are the columns included in the `AnnoOddities.all_stats.tsv` output file:\r
```console\r
FILE: output.AnnoOddities.all_stats.tsv\r
1 transcript_id                             - transcript identifier\r
2 gene_id                                   - gene identifier\r
3 chromosome                                - chromosome name or number\r
4 start                                     - start position\r
5 end                                       - end position\r
6 region                                    - genomic region in the format chr:start-end\r
7 strand                                    - strand information\r
8 exon_num                                  - number of exons\r
9 exons                                     - list of exon positions\r
10 exon_lengths                             - list of exon lengths\r
11 max_exon_length                          - maximum exon length\r
12 min_exon_length                          - minimum exon length\r
13 total_exon_length                        - total length of all exons\r
14 cds_exon_num                             - number of CDS exons\r
15 cds_exons                                - list of CDS exon positions\r
16 cds_exon_lengths                         - list of CDS exon lengths\r
17 max_cds_length                           - maximum CDS exon length\r
18 min_cds_length                           - minimum CDS exon length\r
19 total_cds_length                         - total length of all CDS exons\r
20 cds_cdna_ratio                           - ratio of CDS length to cDNA length\r
21 intron_num                               - number of introns\r
22 introns                                  - list of intron positions\r
23 intron_lengths                           - list of intron lengths\r
24 max_intron_length                        - maximum intron length\r
25 min_intron_length                        - minimum intron length\r
26 total_intron_length                      - total length of all introns\r
27 five_utr_num                             - number of 5' UTRs\r
28 five_utr_length                          - total length of 5' UTRs\r
29 three_utr_num                            - number of 3' UTRs\r
30 three_utr_length                         - total length of 3' UTRs\r
31 has_start_codon                          - presence of start codon\r
32 has_stop_codon                           - presence of stop codon\r
33 is_complete                              - completeness of the transcript\r
34 is_fragment                              - whether the transcript is a fragment\r
35 has_inframe_stop                         - presence of in-frame stop codons\r
36 known_strand_junctions_dict              - dictionary of known strand junctions\r
37 known_strand_junctions_str               - string representation of known strand junctions\r
38 unknown_strand_junctions_dict            - dictionary of unknown strand junctions\r
39 unknown_strand_junctions_str             - string representation of unknown strand junctions\r
40 canonical_intron_count                   - count of canonical introns\r
41 non_canonical_intron_count               - count of non-canonical introns\r
42 suspicious_intron_count                  - count of suspicious introns\r
43 unknown_canonical_intron_count           - count of unknown canonical introns\r
44 unknown_non_canonical_intron_count       - count of unknown non-canonical introns\r
45 unknown_suspicious_intron_count          - count of unknown suspicious introns\r
46 unknown_predicted_strand                 - predicted strand for unknown introns\r
47 canonical_intron_proportion              - proportion of canonical introns\r
48 only_non_canonical_splicing              - whether only non-canonical splicing is present\r
49 suspicious_splicing                      - presence of suspicious splicing\r
50 matched_oddities                         - matched oddities\r
```\r
\r
### AnnoOddities Combined Statistics\r
Consolidated statistics from AGAT, Mikado, GFFread, and AnnoOddities.\r
```console\r
FILE: output.AnnoOddities.combined_statistics.yaml\r
FILE: output.AnnoOddities.combined_statistics.json\r
FILE: output.AnnoOddities.combined_statistics.toml\r
```\r
\r
### AnnoOddities Individual Oddity GFFs\r
Separate GFF3 files for each detected oddity, facilitating targeted review and analysis.\r
```console\r
DIRECTORY: oddity_files\r
FILE: output.AnnoOddities.has_inframe_stop.gff\r
FILE: output.AnnoOddities.max_exon_length_gt_10000.gff\r
FILE: output.AnnoOddities.min_exon_length_lte_5.gff\r
FILE: output.AnnoOddities.exon_num_eq_1.gff\r
FILE: output.AnnoOddities.exon_num_gt_1.gff\r
FILE: output.AnnoOddities.is_fragment.gff\r
FILE: output.AnnoOddities.not_has_start_codon.gff\r
FILE: output.AnnoOddities.not_has_stop_codon.gff\r
FILE: output.AnnoOddities.not_is_complete.gff\r
FILE: output.AnnoOddities.selected_cds_fraction_lte_0.3.gff\r
```\r
\r
### AnnoOddities GFF File\r
A GFF3 file containing all transcripts annotated with their respective oddities. The oddities are included in the attributes column for easy identification, appeneded to the 'Note' field to the respective transcript entries.\r
```console\r
FILE: output.AnnoOddities.gff\r
```\r
