    ns1:dateCreated "2026-02-04" ;
    ns1:dateModified "2026-02-04" ;
    ns1:description """# SMIntegration : Spatial Multi-omics Integration Platform\r
## Introduction\r
**SMIntegration** is an innovative open-source platform for integrated analysis of spatial transcriptomics and metabolomics data. It integrates spatial pattern recognition, differential comparison, network construction, and functional annotation into a unified workflow. Designed to address key challenges in spatial multi-omics correlation analysis, SMIntegration enables researchers to explore gene-metabolite co-regulation mechanisms through an intuitive web interface, revealing spatial heterogeneity in tissue development and disease progression.\r
\r
## Key Features\r
### ?? **Spatial Pattern Discovery**\r
  - Automated identification of spatial expression patterns for genes/metabolites\r
  - Moran's I correlation analysis between transcriptomic/metabolomic modules\r
### ?? **Pixel-level Clustering & Cell Annotation**\r
  - 4 clustering algorithms: Seurat-LV, Seurat-LM, Seurat-SLM, UMAP-kmeans\r
  - SingleR-based automatic cell type annotation with reference datasets\r
  - Custom cell type annotation support\r
### ⚖️ **Flexible Differential Analysis**\r
  - ROI selection via: \r
    - Interactive tissue imaging\r
    - Clustering results \r
    - Cell annotation mapping\r
  - Differentially expressed genes (DEGs) and metabolites (DAMs) detection\r
  - Group-specific gene-metabolite correlation networks\r
### ?? **Functional Enrichment**\r
  - KEGG pathway co-enrichment analysis\r
  - Fisher's exact test for DEG-DAM pathway associations\r
### ?? **Interactive Visualization**\r
  - Gene-metabolite co-localization analysis\r
  - RGB overlay imaging for multi-feature visualization\r
\r
## Getting Started\r
\r
### ?? Online Access  \r
Access the live platform without installation:\r
?? [[[https://metax.genomics.cn/app/SMIntegration](https://metax.genomics.cn/app/smintegration)]\r
\r
### ?? Local Deployment (Docker)  \r
?? [[[Docker Installation Guide](https://docs.docker.com/get-started/get-docker/)]\r
```bash\r
# Pull the latest Docker image\r
docker pull mzlabresearch/smintegration:v-1.0\r
\r
# Run with ShinyProxy\r
docker run -d -p 8787:3838  mzlabresearch/smintegration:v-1.0\r
```\r
Please use a web browser to access: http://localhost:8787\r
\r
### ?? Input Data Format\r
SMIntegration requires two **feature matrices** as input files:\r
\r
**Key Requirements**:\r
\r
1、Pre-aligned datasets\r
Spatial metabolomics + transcriptomics must share identical pixel coordinates，we recommend using [SpatialData](SpatialData.md) for registration.\r
\r
2、Supported Formats:\r
SMIntegration requires two **feature matrices** in TXT or RDS format:\r
\r
**TXT Format**:\r
  - Columns 1-4: Feature name (metabolite or gene), pixel coordinates (x, y), feature abundance (Intensity or MIDCount)\r
  - Each row represents one spatial pixel\r
\r
**RDS Format (Seurat object)**:\r
  - Spatial location information stored in meta.data (x, y)\r
  - Feature matrix stored in data@assays$Spatial (Format: Features as rows, spatial pixels as columns, values represent feature abundance)\r
> ?? Detailed formatting guide available in-app (Tutorial Panel → Data Preparation)\r
\r
## Usage Workflow\r
\r
1. **Upload Data**: Import feature matrix in **Overall Distribution Analysis** Panel\r
2. **Core Analysis**: \r
 - Pattern Recognition: Identify spatial expression modules\r
 - Pixel Clustering: Group pixels using 4 algorithms\r
 - Cell Annotation: Automated (SingleR) or manual mapping\r
 - Differential Analysis: Compare regions (manual/automatic ROI selection)\r
 - Network Construction: Build condition-specific gene-metabolite networks\r
 - Functional Enrichment: Pathway mapping and co-enrichment analysis\r
 - Visualization：Dynamic exploration of spatial distributions and co-localization patterns\r
\r
## Example Data\r
\r
Test dataset: **Mouse brain coronal adjacent sections**\r
1. **Spatial Transcriptomics Data**: \r
 - Acquisition & Processing: Stereo-seq, 0.05μm resolution, aggregated to 50μm resolution\r
 - Content: 14,530 pixels × 500 genes\r
2. **Spatial Metabolomics Data**: \r
 - Acquisition & Processing: AFADESI (+) mode, 50μm resolution, spatially registered to identical pixel coordinates\r
 - Content: 14,530 pixels × 500 metabolites\r
\r
Access:\r
Built-in dataset in SMIntegration (Tutorial Panel → Example Data)\r
\r
Raw data: NGDC OMIX Repository ID: [OMIX011674](https://ngdc.cncb.ac.cn/omix/release/OMIX011674)\r
\r
    \r
## Community & Support\r
\r
Developed by Haoke Deng (denghaoke\\@genomics.cn)\\\r
Last update: 2025-08-11\r
""" ;
