SMIntegration requires two **feature matrices** in TXT or RDS format:\r
\r
**TXT Format**:\r
  - Columns 1-4: Feature name (metabolite or gene), pixel coordinates (x, y), feature abundance (Intensity or MIDCount)\r
  - Each row represents one spatial pixel\r
\r
**RDS Format (Seurat object)**:\r
  - Spatial location information stored in meta.data (x, y)\r
  - Feature matrix stored in data@assays$Spatial (Format: Features as rows, spatial pixels as columns, values represent feature abundance)\r
> ?? Detailed formatting guide available in-app (Tutorial Panel → Data Preparation)\r
\r
## Usage Workflow\r
\r
1. **Upload Data**: Import feature matrix in **Overall Distribution Analysis** Panel\r
2. **Core Analysis**: \r
 - Pattern Recognition: Identify spatial expression modules\r
 - Pixel Clustering: Group pixels using 4 algorithms\r
 - Cell Annotation: Automated (SingleR) or manual mapping\r
 - Differential Analysis: Compare regions (manual/automatic ROI selection)\r
 - Network Construction: Build condition-specific gene-metabolite networks\r
 - Functional Enrichment: Pathway mapping and co-enrichment analysis\r
 - Visualization：Dynamic exploration of spatial distributions and co-localization patterns\r
\r
## Example Data\r
\r
Test dataset: **Mouse brain coronal adjacent sections**\r
1. **Spatial Transcriptomics Data**: \r
 - Acquisition & Processing: Stereo-seq, 0.05μm resolution, aggregated to 50μm resolution\r
 - Content: 14,530 pixels × 500 genes\r
2. **Spatial Metabolomics Data**: \r
 - Acquisition & Processing: AFADESI (+) mode, 50μm resolution, spatially registered to identical pixel coordinates\r
 - Content: 14,530 pixels × 500 metabolites\r
\r
Access:\r
Built-in dataset in SMIntegration (Tutorial Panel → Example Data)\r
\r
Raw data: NGDC OMIX Repository ID: [OMIX011674](https://ngdc.cncb.ac.cn/omix/release/OMIX011674)\r
\r
    \r
## Community & Support\r
