    ns1:description """The Human–AI Ledger (HAIL) defines a structured, repeatable workflow for\r
human–AI collaboration. Through standardized checkpoints and a session ledger,\r
HAIL documents ethical, creative, and procedural context across both human\r
and AI contributions. While AI-generated outputs are inherently non-deterministic,\r
HAIL supports process reproducibility by providing a consistent framework for\r
recording collaboration, facilitating auditability, transparency, and ethical\r
accountability in co-creative AI sessions.\r
\r
The workflow comprises three normative phases:\r
  1. Sign-On              — Seed Block + Goal Statement initialization\r
  2. Iterative Collaboration — standardized Checkpoint Prompts and summaries\r
  3. Sign-Off & Validation  — Final Reflection, Session Ledger compilation, validation\r
\r
Source:  https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17597705\r
License: CC BY 4.0\r
Author:  Evan P. Troendle (ORCID: 0000-0003-4825-4088), Queen's University Belfast\r
Schema:  HAIL_Schema_v1.0.yaml\r
""" ;
