<https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/2153?version=1> a ns1:ComputationalWorkflow ;
    dcterms:conformsTo "https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalWorkflow/1.0-RELEASE" ;
    ns1:applicationSubCategory <http://edamontology.org/topic_3305>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3344>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_4021> ;
    ns1:citation "10.48546/workflowhub.workflow.2153.1" ;
    ns1:creator "Casper de Visser" ;
    ns1:dateCreated "2026-03-27" ;
    ns1:dateModified "2026-05-13" ;
    ns1:description """# EATRIS-Plus Multi-omics Analysis Workflow\r
Analysis workflow used to analyze the cohort of healthy blood donors\r
\r
\r
# Prerequisites\r
\r
### Multi-omics data set from Zenodo\r
- The data is stored in a Multi_Assay_Experiment object, which is used as input for the workflow\r
- The object can be downloaded here: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10782799\r
\r
\r
###  Install Nextflow using conda\r
\r
 **Create a Conda Environment:** \r
```bash\r
   conda create -n nextflow-env\r
   conda activate nextflow-env\r
   conda install -c bioconda nextflow\r
```\r
\r
See also https://anaconda.org/bioconda/nextflow and https://docs.conda.io/projects/conda/en/latest/user-guide/tasks/manage-environments.html.\r
\r
### Singularity\r
\r
For detailed Singularity installation instructions, please refer to the official [Singularity installation guide](https://docs.sylabs.io/guides/3.0/user-guide/installation.html).\r
\r
\r
### Software containers\r
All software containers used in this workflow [can be obtained here](https://github.com/Xomics/Docker_containers) \r
\r
\r
# Execute Analysis Workflow\r
\r
For more instructions on how to run the workflow:\r
```\r
nextflow run main.nf --help\r
```\r
\r
The typical command to run the workflow is:\r
```\r
nextflow run main.nf \r
 	-c dre.config \r
	--config_file config.yml\r
	--references references.bib \r
	--mae_object /dir/MAE_object\r
	--container_dir /dir/containers/\r
	--output dir/of/choice\r
```\r
\r
\r
## Run time\r
This workflow was tested on a Linux environment with 16 CPU cores and 32 GB RAM available.\r
For this hardware, the run times recorded for the individual Nextflow processes are documented [here](/RunTest/execution_trace_2025-12-05.txt)\r
""" ;
    ns1:identifier "2153" ;
    ns1:license "MIT" ;
    ns1:name "EATRIS-Plus Multi-omics Analysis Workflow" ;
    ns1:url <https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/2153?version=1> ;
    ns1:version "1" .

<https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/2154?version=1> a ns1:ComputationalWorkflow ;
    dcterms:conformsTo "https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalWorkflow/1.0-RELEASE" ;
    ns1:citation "10.48546/workflowhub.workflow.2154.1" ;
    ns1:creator "Casper de Visser" ;
    ns1:dateCreated "2026-03-27" ;
    ns1:dateModified "2026-03-27" ;
    ns1:description """# iPSC Data Analysis\r
\r
## Description\r
This project is part of the Dutch X-omics initiative and focuses on the analysis of multi-omics data from several iPSC lines. The data included genomics, transcriptomics, proteomics, and several different types of metabolomics.\r
\r
## Goal\r
The goal is to identify disease-specific traits of the patient-derived iPSC compared to various control lines.\r
\r
## Pipeline overview\r
\r
\r
## File outline\r
|- [README.md](README.md) &emsp;&emsp;&emsp;&emsp;# This readme\\\r
|- [Data analysis plan.md](Data_analysis_plan.md) # Description of the data analysis plan (DAP)\\\r
|- [DAP.png](DAP.png) &emsp;&emsp;&emsp;&emsp;&emsp;&ensp; # Overview image of step 4 and 5 of the DAP\r
\r
## Software and packages used\r
- R version 4.3.2 in the <a href= "file:///Z:/software/R"> software folder </a>\r
(Z:\\software\\R)\r
\r
\r
## Data sources\r
- <a href= "file:///Z:/data/iPSC_data/iPSC_CNV-WES/README.md"> CNV WES </a> (Z:\\data\\iPSC_data\\iPSC_CNV-WES\\README.md)\r
- <a href= "file:///Z:/data/iPSC_data/iPSC_RNAseq/README.md"> RNA-seq </a> (Z:\\data\\iPSC_data\\iPSC_RNAseq\\README.md)\r
- <a href= "file:///Z:/data/iPSC_data/iPSC_proteomics/README.md"> Proteomics </a> (Z:\\data\\iPSC_data\\iPSC_proteomics\\README.md)\r
- <a href= "file:///Z:/data/iPSC_data/iPSC_metabolomics_TML/README.md"> Metabolomics (RUMC, Nijmegen) </a> (Z:\\data\\iPSC_data\\iPSC_metabolomics_TML\\README.md)\r
- <a href= "file:///Z:/data/iPSC_data/iPSC_metabolomics_lipidomics_LUMC/README.md"> Metabolomics and Lipidomics (LUMC, Leiden) </a> (Z:\\data\\iPSC_data\\iPSC_metabolomics_lipidomics_LUMC\\README.md)\r
\r
\r
## Digital Reserarch Environment:\r
\r
#### Support MyDRE:\r
* https://support.mydre.org/\r
\r
#### Gitlab-DRE connection errors\r
If Gitlab gives a timeout warning when used from within the DRE:\r
\r
1) Confirm if https://gitlab.cmbi.umcn.nl/x-omics_ipscs/ipsc-data-analysis.git/ can be accessed through the browser\r
2) Correct the proxy configuration with the following git command:\r
\r
    ````git config --global http.proxy http://proxy.mydre.org:3128````\r
\r
#### CRAN/Bioconductor\r
* Configuration instructions https://support.mydre.org/portal/en/kb/articles/proxy-configurations-rstudio#Introduction\r
\r
Use a Biconductor mirror:\r
* Add `options(BioC_mirror = "https://ftp.gwdg.de/pub/misc/bioconductor/")` to the `C:\\Program Files\\R\\R-[your R version]\\etc\\Rprofile.site`(requires DRE admin rights)\r
\r
## Nextflow workflow\r
Run the analysis workflow using Nextflow\r
\r
\r
Example run command:\r
```\r
nextflow run main.nf \r
	--mae_object path/to/h5MAE/ \r
	--output output/dir \r
	--r_config bin/Analysis/config.yml \r
	--isa_file path/to/20240822_Xomics_iPSC_Neurons_new_READ-ONLY.xlsx \r
	--markers_dir path/to/Markers_files/\r
	--alt_omics_dir path/to/iPSC_MAE/\r
```\r
\r
\r
\r
Example run command in Digital Research Environment (DRE):\r
* Need to specify dre.config and container_dir wit .sif files\r
```\r
nextflow run main.nf \r
	--mae_object /mnt/data/data/iPSC_data/iPSC_MAE/h5MAE/ \r
	-c dre.config \r
	--container_dir /mnt/data/software/singularity/ \r
	--output /output/dir \r
	--r_config bin/Analysis/config.yml \r
	--isa_file /mnt/data/data/iPSC_data/iPSC_MAE/20240822_Xomics_iPSC_Neurons_new_READ-ONLY.xlsx \r
	--markers_dir /mnt/data/data/iPSC_data/Markers_files/\r
	--meth_dir /mnt/data/data/iPSC_data/Meth_NF_files/\r
	--alt_omics_dir /mnt/data/data/iPSC_data/iPSC_MAE/\r
```\r
\r
## Licenses\r
\r
=======\r
# iPSC Data Analysis\r
\r
## Description\r
This project is part of the Dutch X-omics initiative and focuses on the analysis of multi-omics data from several iPSC lines. The data included genomics, transcriptomics, proteomics, and several different types of metabolomics.\r
