## Introduction\r
\r
**EBI-Metagenomics/envident** EBI-Metagenomic's eDNA analysis pipeline. This pipeline is designed for the analysis of environmental DNA (eDNA) sequencing data, implementing a comprehensive workflow for quality control, primer identification, Amplicon Sequence Variant (ASV) calling and taxonomic profiling using modern bioinformatics tools. Currently the pipeline supports analysis of COI metabarcoding reads.\r
\r
<br>\r
<p align="center">\r
  <img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EBI-Metagenomics/envIdent/main/docs/envident_schema.svg" width="900">\r
</p>\r
<br>\r
\r
### Default steps in EnvIdent\r
\r
Quality Control and Preprocessing:\r
* Raw reads quality assessment using FastQC\r
* Reads quality control and filtering using fastp\r
* Minimum read count filtering (configurable threshold)\r
\r
Primer Analysis:\r
* Automatic primer identification using PIMENTO\r
* Primer trimming using Cutadapt\r
* Primer validation and reporting\r
\r
Taxonomic Profiling:\r
* Pfam-based COI (Cytochrome C Oxidase subunit I) profiling using HMMER\r
* Reads percentage threshold filtering for marker gene identification (configurable threshold)\r
\r
ASV Analysis:\r
* Amplicon Sequence Variant (ASV) calling using DADA2\r
* ASV taxonomic classification using MAPseq\r
* Krona chart visualization for taxonomic results\r
\r
Reporting and Quality Control:\r
* Comprehensive MultiQC reports\r
* Failed and passed runs tracking\r
* Software version reporting\r
\r
## Usage\r
\r
> [!NOTE]\r
> If you are new to Nextflow and nf-core, please refer to [this page](https://nf-co.re/docs/usage/installation) on how to set-up Nextflow. Make sure to [test your setup](https://nf-co.re/docs/usage/introduction#how-to-run-a-pipeline) with `-profile test` before running the workflow on actual data.\r
\r
### Requirements\r
\r
The pipeline requires:\r
\r
* Nextflow (≥24.04.2)\r
* Docker, Singularity, or Conda for software management\r
* Access to reference databases\r
* Primer database formatted for PIMENTO - a FASTA file with contig ids ending with F for forward primers and R for reverse primers. See [here](https://github.com/EBI-Metagenomics/PIMENTO/blob/main/pimento/standard_primers/V3-V5.fasta) for an example\r
\r
### Input Format\r
\r
The input data should be eDNA sequencing reads (paired-end or single-end) in FASTQ format, specified using a CSV samplesheet:\r
\r
```\r
sample,fastq_1,fastq_2,single_end\r
sample1,/path/to/sample1_R1.fastq.gz,/path/to/sample1_R2.fastq.gz,false\r
sample2,/path/to/sample2.fastq.gz,,true\r
```\r
\r
### Basic execution\r
\r
```\r
nextflow run EBI-Metagenomics/envident \\\r
    -r main \\\r
    -profile example_slurm \\\r
    --input samplesheet.csv \\\r
    --outdir results\r
```\r
\r
