## Introduction\r
\r
**nf-core/genomeqc** is a bioinformatics pipeline that compares the quality of multiple genomes, along with their annotations.\r
\r
The pipeline takes a list of genomes and annotations (from local files or ncbi accessions), and runs commonly used tools to assess their quality.\r
\r
<picture>\r
   <source media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" srcset="docs/images/nf-core-genomeqc_metro_map_v4_logo_dark.png">\r
   <img alt="nf-core/genomeqc" src="docs/images/nf-core-genomeqc_metro_map_v4.png">\r
</picture>\r
\r
1. Downloads the genome and gene annotation files from NCBI: [NCBI genome download](https://github.com/kblin/ncbi-genome-download) - Or **provide your own genomes and annotations**.\r
2. Describes genome assembly:\r
   1. [BUSCO](https://busco.ezlab.org/): Evaluates genome/proteome completeness based on **single copy markers**.\r
   2. **BUSCO Ideogram**: Plots the location of BUSCO markers on the assembly.\r
   3. [Merqury](https://github.com/marbl/merqury) (optional): Evaluates genome completeness based on sequencing reads.\r
   4. [tidk](https://github.com/tolkit/telomeric-identifier) (optional): Identifies and visualises telomeric repeats.\r
   5. [QUAST](https://github.com/ablab/quast): Computes contiguity and integrity statistics: N50, N90, GC%, number of sequences.\r
   6. Contamination screening:\r
      - [FCS-GX](https://github.com/ncbi/fcs/wiki/FCS-GX-quickstart): Detection and removal of foreign organisms contamination.\r
      - [FCS-adaptor](https://github.com/ncbi/fcs/wiki/FCS-adaptor-quickstart): Detection and removal of adaptor and vector contamination.\r
      - [Tiara](https://ibe-uw.github.io/tiara/): DNA sequence classification.\r
   7. TE annotation (optional, `--te`):\r
      - [`--te hite`](https://github.com/BioinformaticsToolsmith/HiTE): Fast, alignment-free TE identification and masking.\r
      - `--te repeatmasker`: Curated TE masking using [DFAM famdb](https://www.dfam.org) + [RepeatMasker](https://www.repeatmasker.org). Add `--run_repeatmodeler` to also build a de novo library with [RepeatModeler](https://www.repeatmasker.org/RepeatModeler/) (slow — 24–48 h per genome). The repeat library is dereplicated using [MMseqs2](https://github.com/soedinglab/MMseqs2) `easy-linclust` by default; use `--te_clusterer` to switch tools and `--te_cluster_identity`/`--te_cluster_coverage` to tune thresholds. RepeatMasker runs in rush mode (`-qq`) by default; use `--repeatmasker_speed` to adjust.\r
3. Describes annotation:\r
   1. [AGAT](https://agat.readthedocs.io/en/latest/): Number of genes, features, length...\r
   2. **Gene Overlaps**: Finds the number of overlapping genes.\r
4. Extracts longest protein isoform: [GffRead](https://github.com/gpertea/gffread).\r
5. Finds orthologous genes: [Orthofinder](https://github.com/davidemms/OrthoFinder).\r
6. Plots an orthology-based - if annotation is given - or BUSCO marker-based - if no annotation is given - phylogenetic tree with summary statistics: **Tree Summary**. Selectable `--tree_style`: a conventional left-to-right tree, or a **circular** layout with the summary statistics drawn as concentric rings and quality metrics scored as a colour-blind-safe Good/Warn/Poor traffic light.\r
7. Summary with **HTML and excel** custom reports.\r
8. Summary with [MultiQC](http://multiqc.info).\r
\r
The pipeline outputs an executable that launches a shiny app with the tree plot and the summary statistics. The parameters of the plot can be modified, and summary statistics can be added or removed in real time. Once the plot has been adjusted, it can be saved as png/svg. The tree plot needs **at least three assemblies to be plotted**, and it servers as a quick overview of the quality of all assemblies.\r
\r
If **no annotation** is given as input, the pipeline will ignore the steps **involving gene statistics**.\r
\r
> [!WARNING]\r
> We strongly suggest users to specify the lineage using the `--busco_lineage` parameter, as setting the lineage to `auto` (default value) might cause problems with `BUSCO` during the lineage determination step.\r
\r
> [!NOTE]\r
> `BUSCO Ideogram` will only plot those chromosomes -or scaffolds- that contain at least one single copy marker.\r
\r
## Usage\r
\r
> [!NOTE]\r
> If you are new to Nextflow and nf-core, please refer to [this page](https://nf-co.re/docs/get_started/environment_setup/overview) on how to set-up Nextflow. Make sure to [test your setup](https://nf-co.re/docs/get_started/run-your-first-pipeline) with `-profile test` before running the workflow on actual data.\r
\r
First, prepare an input **samplesheet** in **csv format** (e.g. `samplesheet.csv`). You can prepare your sampplesheet using:\r
\r
### 1. Local files\r
\r
Simply point out to your local genome assembly and annotation (in FASTA and GFF format, respectively) using the `fasta` and `gff` fields:\r
\r
```csv\r
assembly,fasta,gff\r
assembly_1,/path/to/genome1.fasta,/path/to/annotation1.gff3\r
assembly_2,/path/to/genome2.fasta,/path/to/annotation2.gff3\r
assembly_3,/path/to/genome3.fasta,/path/to/annotation3.gff3\r
```\r
\r
### 2. ncbi accessions\r
\r
Additionally, you can run the pipeline providing ncbi accessions (RefSeq or GenBank, depeding on the mode you wish to run) in the `ncbi` field:\r
\r
```csv\r
assembly,ncbi\r
assembly_1,GCF_000000001.1\r
assembly_2,GCF_000000002.1\r
assembly_3,GCF_000000003.1\r
```\r
\r
### 3. Both\r
\r
You can combine both input types in the same samplesheet:\r
\r
```csv\r
assembly,ncbi,fasta,gff\r
assembly_1,GCF_000000001.1\r
assembly_2,,/path/to/genome2.fasta,/path/to/annotation2.gff3\r
assembly_3,GCF_000000003.1\r
assembly_4,,/path/to/genome4.fasta,/path/to/annotation4.gff3\r
```\r
\r
### Run the pipeline\r
\r
Run the pipeline using:\r
\r
```bash\r
nextflow run nf-core/genomeqc \\\r
   -profile <docker/singularity/.../institute> \\\r
   --input samplesheet.csv \\\r
   --outdir <OUTDIR>\r
```\r
\r
You can run the pipeline using a test profile and docker:\r
\r
```bash\r
nextflow run nf-core/genomeqc -profile test,docker --outdir ./results\r
```\r
\r
> [!WARNING]\r
> Please provide pipeline parameters via the CLI or Nextflow `-params-file` option. Custom config files including those provided by the `-c` Nextflow option can be used to provide any configuration _**except for parameters**_; see [docs](https://nf-co.re/docs/running/run-pipelines#using-parameter-files).\r
\r
For more details and further functionality, please refer to the [usage documentation](https://nf-co.re/genomeqc/usage) and the [parameter documentation](https://nf-co.re/genomeqc/parameters).\r
\r
## Pipeline output\r
\r
To see the results of an example test run with a full size dataset refer to the [results](https://nf-co.re/genomeqc/results) tab on the nf-core website pipeline page.\r
For more details about the output files and reports, please refer to the\r
[output documentation](https://nf-co.re/genomeqc/output).\r
\r
