    ns1:description """# Phorager\r
  ### Prophage Analysis Pipeline\r
\r
  A comprehensive pipeline for bacterial genome quality control, prophage detection, and prophage characterization\r
\r
**Authors:**  \r
\r
- Xena Dyball\r
- James Docherty\r
- [Alise Ponsero](https://github.com/aponsero)\r
- Ryan Cook\r
\r
**Citation:**\r
[Paper Citation or Preprint Link]\r
\r
## Overview\r
\r
Phorager provides an integrated workflow for:\r
\r
- **Bacterial genome quality control** - CheckM2 assessment, filtering, and dRep dereplication\r
- **Prophage detection** - GenoMAD and VIBRANT-based identification of integrated prophages\r
- **Phage annotation** - CheckV quality assessment, Pharokka annotation, and Phold function prediction\r
- **Summary tables** - Structured TSV summaries of QC metrics and prophage characteristics across your dataset\r
\r
> **Note**: Phorager is currently in beta release. We welcome feedback, bug reports, and feature requests through our [issue tracker](../../issues).\r
\r
## Quick Start\r
\r
### 1. Configure\r
Set your preferred installation backend and locations:\r
\r
```bash\r
phorager config set --backend conda --db-location /data/phorager\r
```\r
\r
### 2. Install\r
Install required tools and databases:\r
\r
```bash\r
# Install tools for bacterial genome analysis\r
phorager install --tools genome --databases checkm2\r
\r
# Install prophage detection tools\r
phorager install --tools prophage --databases genomad,vibrant\r
```\r
\r
### 3. Run Analysis\r
Execute workflows on your data:\r
\r
```bash\r
# Bacterial genome quality control\r
phorager bacterial --genome /path/to/genomes --outdir results/\r
\r
# Prophage detection\r
phorager prophage --genome /path/to/genomes --outdir results/\r
\r
# Prophage annotation and clustering\r
phorager annotation --prophage results/ --outdir results/\r
```\r
\r
### 4. Generate Summaries\r
Create structured summary tables from your completed results:\r
\r
```bash\r
# Bacterial genome QC metrics with prophage counts\r
phorager summarize --type bacterial_genome --outdir results/\r
\r
# Per-prophage table with host, cluster, quality, and annotation\r
phorager summarize --type prophage_table --outdir results/\r
```\r
\r
Output is written to `results/4.Summaries/`. Use `phorager summarize --list` to see all available summary types.\r
\r
## Prerequisites\r
\r
- [Nextflow](https://www.nextflow.io/) (≥ 21.04.0)\r
- Either [Conda/Mamba](https://docs.conda.io/en/latest/) or [Singularity](https://sylabs.io/singularity/)\r
\r
## Documentation\r
\r
**For detailed documentation, see the [Wiki](../../wiki):**\r
\r
- [Configuration](../../wiki/Configuration) - Backend setup and locations\r
- [Installation](../../wiki/Installation) - Tools and database installation\r
- [Bacterial Workflow](../../wiki/Bacterial-Workflow) - Genome quality control and dereplication\r
- [Prophage Workflow](../../wiki/Prophage-Workflow) - Integrated prophage detection\r
- [Annotation Workflow](../../wiki/Annotation-Workflow) - Prophage annotation and clustering\r
- [Summary Workflow](../../wiki/Summary-Workflow) - Generating summary tables from pipeline outputs\r
\r
## Getting Help\r
\r
- Check command-specific help: `phorager [command] --help`\r
- View available tools and databases: `phorager install --list-available`\r
- Preview commands before running: `phorager [command] --dry-run`\r
- See current configuration: `phorager config show`\r
- List available summary types: `phorager summarize --list`\r
\r
## Reporting Issues and Feedback\r
\r
Phorager is actively being developed and improved. We encourage users to:\r
\r
- **Report bugs** - Found an issue? [Open a bug report](../../issues/new)\r
- **Request features** - Have an idea for improvement? [Submit a feature request](../../issues/new)\r
- **Ask questions** - Need help? [Start a discussion](../../issues/new)\r
- **Share feedback** - Let us know about your experience using Phorager\r
\r
When reporting issues, please include:\r
- Command used\r
- Error messages or unexpected behavior\r
- Phorager version and backend (conda/singularity)\r
- System information (OS, available resources)\r
\r
""" ;
