\r
# Bioimaging Data Management Workflow for Plasma Medicine\r
This repository contains the Jupyter notebook implementation of a bioimaging data management workflow for plasma medicine (see [Sci Data paper](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-026-07982-x ) and [poster](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.16412003)). The workflow is implemented as a structured pipeline integrating open-source tools, including  [OMERO](https://www.openmicroscopy.org/omero/) for image data management, [eLabFTW](https://www.elabftw.net/) as an electronic laboratory notebook, [Adamant](https://github.com/plasma-mds/adamant) for schema-driven metadata collection, and [Micro-Meta App](https://wu-bimac.github.io/MicroMetaApp.github.io/) for standardized documentation of microscopy acquisition settings that are connected via programming interfaces to enable persistent linkage of metadata to image datasets using standardized annotations.\r
\r
<!--\r
## Changelog\r
### [x.x.x] January 26, 2026\r
* Initial release of the GitHub repository\r
-->\r
\r
## Set up\r
A [JupyterLab](https://jupyter.org) environment is required to run the provided [notebook](workflow.ipynb).\r
The workflow was designed and tested on Python 3.12.5.\r
Follow the [installation guideline](https://jupyter.org/install) for support.\r
\r
## Dependencies \r
The following list summarizes the key dependencies:\r
* [**Elabapi**](https://pypi.org/project/elabapi-python/)\r
* [**OMERO-py**](https://pypi.org/project/omero-py/)\r
* [**Openpyxl**](https://pypi.org/project/openpyxl/)\r
* [**Pandas**](https://pypi.org/project/pandas/)\r
\r
## Usage\r
To use the provided Jupyter notebook, download [workflow.ipynb](workflow.ipynb) and the two Python scripts [omerohandler.py](scripts/omerohandler.py) and [elabftwapihandler.py](scripts/elabftwapihandler.py).\r
These files must be located in the same working directory.\r
To access the respective OMERO and eLabFTW instances, the host addresses must be adjusted in the respective handler scripts (see description below).\r
\r
### eLabFTW\r
The codeline (l. 43) in elabftwapihandler.py has to be changed:\r
```\r
configuration.host = 'hostAdress'\r
```\r
the 'hostAdress' variable has to be replaced by the actual host url adress of your eLabFTW instance.\r
\r
### OMERO\r
The codeline (l. 21) in omerohandler.py has to be changed:\r
```\r
conn = BlitzGateway(usrname, passwrd, host= hostAdress, port= hostPort, secure=True)\r
```\r
the 'hostAdress' variable has to be replaced by the actual host url adress of your OMERO instance.\r
\r
The adjusted notebook can be accessed by opening the .ipynb file in a JupyterLab environment; in some local JupyterLab installations, double-clicking the downloaded, modified .ipynb file may be sufficient.\r
\r
## Support\r
If you find a bug or need help, please open an issue. When reporting a bug, include the version, OS, steps to reproduce, expected vs actual behavior, and any logs or screenshots.\r
\r
## How to cite\r
Ahmadi, M., Wagner, R., Bekeschus, S. et al. Data Management Workflow for FAIR Sharing of Bioimaging Datasets in Plasma Medicine. Sci Data 13, 1124 (2026). https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-026-07982-x \r
\r
