<https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/2248?version=1> a ns1:ComputationalWorkflow ;
    dcterms:conformsTo "https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalWorkflow/1.0-RELEASE" ;
    ns1:citation "" ;
    ns1:dateCreated "2026-08-24" ;
    ns1:dateModified "2026-08-24" ;
    ns1:description """# SciWIn-Client Demo\r
This repo contains the scripts to perform a small SciWIn-Client Demo. This instructions file will be updated to use new features when they are available. The commands stated below will perform the operations based on our [hello world repo](https://github.com/fairagro/m4.4_hello_world).\r
\r
![](https://github.com/fairagro/m4.4_sciwin_client_demo_ta4_retreat_2024/blob/complete_run/workflow.svg)\r
\r
## Demo Commands\r
To check if SciWIn is available type `s4n --version` which should output something like `s4n 1.0.0`.\r
### Initializing a Project\r
To begin the journey use `s4n init` to initialize a project in the current directory.\r
```bash\r
s4n init\r
```\r
Create a virtual environment\r
```bash\r
python -m venv .venv\r
source .venv/bin/activate\r
pip install -r requirements.txt\r
```\r
### Creation of CommandLineTools\r
To create the two CommandLineTools needed for the demo you just have to prefix the execution commands with `s4n create`.\r
#### Calculation\r
To create the `calculation.cwl` tool run the following command:\r
```bash\r
s4n create python calculation.py --population population.csv --speakers speakers.csv\r
```\r
which will output something like\r
```\r
?? The current working directory is /home/ubuntu/sciwin_test\r
▶️  Executing command: python calculation.py --population population.csv --speakers speakers.csv\r
Total population: 7694245029\r
            language    speakers  percentage\r
0             Bangla   300000000    3.899018\r
1    Egyptian Arabic   100542400    1.306722\r
2            English  1132366680   14.717060\r
3             German   134993040    1.754468\r
4         Indonesian   198996550    2.586304\r
5           Japanese   128000000    1.663581\r
6         Portuguese   475300000    6.177344\r
7            Punjabi   125000000    1.624591\r
8            Russian   154000000    2.001496\r
9  Standard Mandarin  1090951810   14.178803\r
\r
?? Found changes:\r
        - results.csv\r
\r
?? Created CWL file workflows/calculation/calculation.cwl\r
```\r
#### Plot\r
The Plot tool will use the created results.csv. The creation command is \r
```bash\r
s4n create python plot.py --results results.csv\r
```\r
which will lead to the following output:\r
```\r
?? The current working directory is /home/ubuntu/sciwin_test\r
▶️  Executing command: python plot.py --results results.csv\r
\r
?? Found changes:\r
        - results.svg\r
\r
?? Created CWL file workflows/plot/plot.cwl\r
```\r
### Workflow Creation\r
#### Workflow Creation\r
To create a Workflow with name `demo` simply call. However this is optional as it will be executed automatically upon running the `connect` command the first time.\r
```bash\r
s4n create --name demo\r
```\r
which will output\r
```\r
?? Created new Workflow file: workflows/demo/demo.cwl\r
```\r
\r
#### Connecting Tools\r
To connect the steps in the workflow you need to call `s4n connect` a couple of times.\r
\r
##### Connecting Inputs\r
First we will connect the `calculation` tool to the input sockets. The tool has two inputs which we will connect to the `speaker`s and `pop` input.\r
```bash\r
s4n connect demo --from @inputs/speakers --to calculation/speakers\r
s4n connect demo --from @inputs/pop --to calculation/population\r
```\r
An example output looks like\r
```\r
➕ Added step calculation to workflow\r
➕ Added or updated connection from inputs.speakers to calculation/speakers in workflow\r
✔️  Updated Workflow workflows/demo/demo.cwl!\r
```\r
\r
##### Connecting Tools\r
We now will connect the `plot` and the `calculation` tool. We will map results-output to results-input.\r
```bash\r
s4n connect demo --from calculation/results --to plot/results\r
```\r
An example output looks like\r
```\r
?? Found step calculation in workflow. Not changing that!\r
➕ Added step plot to workflow\r
✔️  Updated Workflow workflows/demo/demo.cwl!\r
```\r
\r
##### Connecting to output\r
To get the results file we will connect the result of the plot step to out.\r
```bash\r
s4n connect demo --from plot/o_results --to @outputs/out\r
```\r
which outputs\r
```\r
➕ Added or updated connection from plot/results to outputs.out in workflow!\r
✔️  Updated Workflow workflows/demo/demo.cwl!\r
```\r
\r
To commit a simple call is needed:\r
```bash\r
s4n save demo\r
```\r
\r
We now have a full workflow which can be executed\r
```bash\r
s4n execute local workflows/demo/demo.cwl --pop population.csv --speakers speakers_revised.csv\r
```\r
\r
However we did not use Docker containers, so this will work only on our computer.\r
take a look at the other examples to learn how to use Docker with s4n. https://github.com/fairagro/m4.4_sciwin_client_examples""" ;
    ns1:identifier "2248" ;
