<https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/2300?version=1> a ns1:ComputationalWorkflow ;
    dcterms:conformsTo "https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalWorkflow/1.0-RELEASE" ;
    ns1:citation "10.48546/workflowhub.workflow.2300.1" ;
    ns1:creator "Shixiang Wang" ;
    ns1:dateCreated "2026-09-05" ;
    ns1:dateModified "2026-09-05" ;
    ns1:description "Automated RNA-seq analysis from locally downloaded SRA archives to differential expression results: verify and symlink .sra files, fasterq-dump conversion to FASTQ, read merging across multiple SRR runs per sample, fastp trimming, STAR alignment with gene counts, BAM indexing, BPM-normalized bigWig signal tracks, a merged count matrix, and DESeq2 differential analysis with ashr shrinkage. Every tool is pinned to an exact conda version for reproducibility. Paired- and single-end samples are routed per sample via metadata (sample-group metadata + wildcard-scoped when predicates), and a second entry point (main_encode.oxoflow) covers the upstream ENCODE execution path." ;
    ns1:identifier "2300" ;
    ns1:keywords "bigwig",
        "deseq2",
        "differential-expression",
        "encode",
        "fasterq-dump",
        "fastp",
        "rna-seq",
        "sra",
        "star" ;
    ns1:license "other-open" ;
    ns1:name "SRA-powered RNA-seq: .sra archives to differential expression" ;
    ns1:url <https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/2300?version=1> ;
    ns1:version "1" .

<https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/2301?version=1> a ns1:ComputationalWorkflow ;
    dcterms:conformsTo "https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalWorkflow/1.0-RELEASE" ;
    ns1:citation "10.48546/workflowhub.workflow.2301.1" ;
    ns1:creator "Shixiang Wang" ;
    ns1:dateCreated "2026-09-05" ;
    ns1:dateModified "2026-09-05" ;
    ns1:description "Paired-end RNA-seq from FASTQ to per-sample alternative-splicing calls: reads are trimmed with fastp, aligned with two-pass STAR and counted per gene with featureCounts; each sample's splicing is then quantified independently with four callers — rMATS, MAJIQ (with Voila export), SUPPA2 (via Salmon transcript quantification) and SplAdder. The alignment and AS-calling stages are one chained DAG (run one stage with -t alignment / -t as_calling)." ;
    ns1:identifier "2301" ;
    ns1:keywords "alternative-splicing",
        "majiq",
        "rmats",
        "rna-seq",
        "snakemake",
        "spladder",
        "star",
        "suppa2" ;
    ns1:license "other-open" ;
    ns1:name "Paired-end RNA-seq alignment and four-caller alternative-splicing analysis" ;
    ns1:url <https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/2301?version=1> ;
    ns1:version "1" .

<https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/2302?version=1> a ns1:ComputationalWorkflow ;
    dcterms:conformsTo "https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalWorkflow/1.0-RELEASE" ;
    ns1:citation "" ;
    ns1:dateCreated "2026-09-07" ;
    ns1:dateModified "2026-09-09" ;
    ns1:description """# PanVariants Usage Documentation\r
\r
## Overview\r
`PanVariants` is a highly accurate variant detection pipeline that integrates pangenome references and artificial intelligence (AI) model to identify single nucleotide variants (SNVs), INDELs (<50 bp), copy number variants (CNVs), short tandem repeats (STRs), and other structural variants (SVs, >50 bp). It supports execution on both local machines and Sun Grid Engine (SGE) clusters.\r
\r
## Install\r
```bash\r
git clone https://github.com/MGI-EU/PanVariants.git\r
```\r
\r
### Database download\r
- Here we take the download of databases related to the GRCh38 reference genome as an example; the download process for other reference genomes is similar.\r
```bash\r
sh PanVariants_required_files.sh\r
```\r
\r
### singularity .sif files download\r
- Download all .sif files from this URL: https://zenodo.org/records/19848582 and place them in the "sifs" folder.\r
  \r
### Required Software\r
| Software | Version | Installation |\r
|----------|---------|--------------|\r
| **Nextflow** | 23.10.0 | Download from: `https://github.com/nextflow-io/nextflow/releases/download/v23.10.0/nextflow-23.10.0-all` <br> Rename to `nextflow` and copy to software directory |\r
| **Java** | ≥ 17 | Required for Nextflow execution |\r
| **Singularity** | ≥ 3.8 | Required for containerized execution |\r
| **Python** | ≥ 3.9.13 | Required for running the Python wrapper script |\r
\r
### Optional Software\r
| Software | Description |\r
|----------|-------------|\r
| **SGE (Sun Grid Engine)** | Optional cluster management system for distributed computing (required only for `blc` executor) |\r
### Optional Arguments\r
\r
| Argument | Short | Default | Description |\r
|----------|-------|---------|-------------|\r
| `--output` | `-o` | `result` | Output directory path |\r
| `--reference` | `-ref` | `GRCh38` | Reference genome version. Options: `GRCh38` or `CHM13` |\r
| `--run_cnv` | `-rc` | `yes` | Enable CNV detection (`yes` / `no`) |\r
| `--run_sv` | `-rs` | `yes` | Enable SV detection (`yes` / `no`) |\r
| `--run_str` | `-rstr` | `yes` | Enable STR detection (`yes` / `no`) |\r
| `--mark_dup` | `-md` | `no` | Mark duplicate reads (`yes` / `no`) |\r
| `--fq_filter` | `-ft` | `no` | Run FastQ filtering (`yes` / `no`) |\r
| `--split_bam` | `-sb` | `no` | Split BAM files by chromosome and run DeepVariant per chromosome (`yes` / `no`) |\r
| `--adapter1` | `-ad1` | `AAGTCGGAGGCCAAGCGGTCTTAGGAAGACAA` | Adapter 1 sequence |\r
| `--adapter2` | `-ad2` | `AAGTCGGATCGTAGCCATGTCGTTCTGTGAGCCAAGGAGTTG` | Adapter 2 sequence |\r
| `--re_alignment` | `-ra` | `no` | Perform re-alignment (`yes` / `no`) |\r
| `--nf_config` | `-c` | - | Path to Nextflow configuration file |\r
| `--db` | `-d` | - | Database path |\r
| `--script` | `-sp` | - | Script path |\r
| `--sif` | `-f` | - | Path to Singularity container image (`.sif`) |\r
| `--scratch_tmp` | `-scr` | - | Path for Nextflow scratch directive |\r
| `--queue` | `-q` | - | Queue name for the `qsub -q` parameter. **Note:** Only effective when `--executor` is set to `blc`. |\r
| `--project` | `-pj` | - | Project name for the `qsub -P` parameter. **Note:** Only effective when `--executor` is set to `blc`. |\r
| `--ansi_log` | `-an` | `false` | Enable ANSI logging for Nextflow (`true` / `false`) |\r
| `--help` | `-h` | - | Show help message and exit |\r
\r
## Notes\r
\r
- The `--queue` and `--project` parameters are only valid when `--executor` is set to `blc`.\r
- The sample list file must strictly follow the format: three tab-separated columns with no header row.\r
- Do not run the pipeline from inside the `--output` directory; doing so will cause errors.\r
- If using Singularity containers, ensure the correct `.sif` file path is provided via `-f`.\r
- Duplicate marking and FastQ filtering are disabled by default. Set them explicitly to `yes` if required.\r
\r
---\r
""" ;
    ns1:identifier "2302" ;
    ns1:license "GPL-3.0" ;
    ns1:name "PanVariants: Best Practice for Pangenome-based Variant Calling Pipeline and Framework" ;
    ns1:url <https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/2302?version=1> ;
    ns1:version "1" .

