    ns1:description """# imputation\r
\r
[![DOI](https://zenodo.org/badge/882188659.svg)](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23405367)\r
\r
A Snakemake workflow that takes **measured genotypes** (a VCF, e.g. from the\r
[genotyping](https://github.com/swarbricklab/genotyping) workflow) and prepares\r
them for single-cell demultiplexing by quality-controlling the calls and\r
**imputing** missing variants against a 1000 Genomes reference panel.\r
\r
It contains two workflows that run in sequence:\r
\r
1. **QC** (`Snakefile_qc`, `rules/qc.smk`) — filters samples (missingness,\r
   relatedness), checks reported sex, and assigns ancestry by comparison against\r
   a 1000 Genomes reference.\r
2. **Imputation** (`Snakefile_imputation`, `rules/imputation.smk`) — lifts the\r
   genotypes to GRCh38, harmonises and fixes reference alleles, phases, imputes\r
   missing variants against a 1000 Genomes reference panel, and filters the\r
   result (MAF, imputation R², exonic regions) to produce SNP profiles.\r
\r
These are the second and third stages of the SNP-based demultiplexing pipeline:\r
\r
```\r
[genotyping](https://github.com/swarbricklab/genotyping)  ->  imputation (this repo: QC + imputation)  ->  [snp_demux](https://github.com/swarbricklab/snp_demux) (Demuxafy)\r
```\r
\r
The final VCF of imputed SNP profiles is consumed by the [snp_demux](https://github.com/swarbricklab/snp_demux) workflow which uses\r
[Demuxafy](https://demultiplexing-doublet-detecting-docs.readthedocs.io/) to\r
assign cells to donors in multiplexed 10x Chromium pools.\r
\r
> This workflow was **adapted from the sc-eQTLGen consortium WG1 genotype-QC + imputation\r
> pipeline** (Powell Lab / Garvan;\r
> [sc-eQTLgen-consortium/WG1-pipeline-QC](https://github.com/sc-eQTLgen-consortium/WG1-pipeline-QC)).\r
> See [`docs/UPSTREAM_DIFFERENCES.md`](docs/UPSTREAM_DIFFERENCES.md) for exactly how this\r
> version differs (and how it relates to the Powell Lab's sibling `SNP_imputation_1000g_hg38`).\r
> Citation details are in [`CITATION.cff`](CITATION.cff) and under [Attribution](#attribution) below.\r
\r
## Inputs (from `genotyping`)\r
\r
- **VCF** — genotype calls for all samples (hg19 for QC; hg38 for imputation, used only for chrX/chrY)\r
- **psam** — a sample description file for `plink`\r
- **id map** — maps original sample ids to the `plink`-safe ids in the `.psam`\r
\r
## Outputs\r
\r
- **QC**: a post-QC set of `plink` files (`pgen`/`pvar`/`psam`) with sex\r
  double-checked and ancestry assigned from the 1000 Genomes reference.\r
- **Imputation**: imputed, filtered SNP profiles ready for Demuxafy.\r
\r
## Rule graphs\r
\r
### Plink QC\r
\r
![QC rule graph](docs/qc_rulegraph.svg)\r
\r
### Imputation\r
\r
![Imputation rule graph](docs/imputation_rulegraph.svg)\r
\r
## Tools\r
\r
The rules drive standard population-genetics tooling, each pinned to a specific\r
public version:\r
\r
| Step | Tool | Version |\r
|------|------|---------|\r
| VCF manipulation, reference fixing (`+fixref`) | `bcftools` | 1.10.2 |\r
| QC, ancestry, format conversion | `plink` / `plink2` | 1.90b6.21 / 2.00a3.7 |\r
| Missingness, heterozygosity, site filtering | `vcftools` | 0.1.16 |\r
| Liftover hg19 → GRCh38 | `CrossMap` | 0.6.5 |\r
| Strand/allele harmonisation | `GenotypeHarmonizer` | 1.4.23 |\r
| Phasing | `Eagle` | 2.4.1 |\r
| Imputation | `Minimac4` | 1.0.2 |\r
| Het filter + ancestry-PCA plotting (R scripts) | `R` (`r-base`) | 4.3 |\r
| Initial sample reheader | `bcftools` (biocontainer) | 1.21 |\r
\r
Versions are pinned to those the upstream monolithic `.sif` shipped — see\r
`docs/UPSTREAM_DIFFERENCES.md`.\r
\r
> **Containerised, with a conda fallback.** The former monolithic image\r
> (`SNP_imputation_1000g_hg38.sif`) has been retired. **By default** every rule runs\r
> from a pinned, public per-rule OCI image under\r
> [`ghcr.io/swarbricklab`](https://github.com/orgs/swarbricklab/packages) (built with\r
> [absconda(https://github.com/swarbricklab/absconda)), selected via the `containers:` map in the config; run with\r
> `--use-singularity` (the bundled `nci` profile already does). GenotypeHarmonizer and\r
> Minimac4 (no bioconda package) are baked into their images; the reheader step uses\r
> the public `quay.io/biocontainers/bcftools:1.21` image.\r
>\r
> **No Singularity/Apptainer?** Every rule also carries a commented `conda:` directive\r
> pointing at `workflow/envs/*.yaml` (the same pinned versions). Uncomment the `conda:`\r
> blocks and run with `--use-conda` instead of `--use-singularity` to build the tools\r
> from conda — no container runtime required. See issue #23.\r
\r
## Reference data and provenance\r
\r
All reference data is **public** and tracked via `dvc import-url` from public\r
sources (see the `.dvc` files under `resources/`), so it can be fetched without\r
access to any private registry:\r
\r
- `resources/eQTLGenImpRef.tar.gz` — sceQTL-Gen / Powell Lab bundle (Minimac4\r
  imputation reference, 1000 Genomes 30x-GRCh38 phasing/panel, GRCh38 QC FASTA)\r
- `resources/1000G.tar.gz` — 1000 Genomes phase-3 plink (ancestry QC)\r
- `resources/bed/hg38exonsUCSC.bed` — hg38 exon BED\r
- `resources/liftover/GRCh37_to_GRCh38.chain.gz` — Ensembl GRCh37→GRCh38 liftover chain\r
- `resources/genomes/chr_map/`, `resources/genomes/GRCh38_chr.fai` — small, git-tracked\r
\r
Fetch, then extract into the paths the config/rules expect:\r
\r
```bash\r
# If you have access to the project's DVC remote:\r
dvc pull\r
# Or, without remote access, re-download straight from the public source URLs:\r
dvc update resources/eQTLGenImpRef.tar.gz.dvc resources/1000G.tar.gz.dvc \\\r
           resources/bed/hg38exonsUCSC.bed.dvc \\\r
           resources/liftover/GRCh37_to_GRCh38.chain.gz.dvc\r
\r
./prep.sh    # extract the archives into place; tarballs can then be deleted\r
```\r
\r
## Attribution\r
\r
Adapted from the sc-eQTLGen consortium **WG1 genotype-QC + imputation pipeline**\r
([sc-eQTLgen-consortium/WG1-pipeline-QC](https://github.com/sc-eQTLgen-consortium/WG1-pipeline-QC);\r
Powell Lab / Garvan) — see [`docs/UPSTREAM_DIFFERENCES.md`](docs/UPSTREAM_DIFFERENCES.md) for\r
the differences, including how it relates to the Powell Lab's sibling pipeline\r
`powellgenomicslab/SNP_imputation_1000g_hg38`. The sc-eQTLGen WG1 authors (Powell Lab) have\r
said they are happy for this adapted workflow to be released under the MIT licence with\r
attribution.\r
\r
**If you use this workflow — including in any publication arising from it — please cite the\r
sc-eQTLGen sources, as requested by the WG1 authors:**\r
\r
- Kaptijn *et al.* (2026), *bioRxiv* — the main sc-eQTLGen consortium paper,\r
  "Federated single-cell QTL meta-analysis reveals novel disease mechanisms"\r
  ([doi:10.64898/2026.01.20.700519](https://doi.org/10.64898/2026.01.20.700519)).\r
- van der Wijst *et al.* (2020), *eLife* — the single-cell eQTLGen consortium.\r
- The sc-eQTLGen consortium **WG1 genotype-QC + imputation pipeline** (the upstream source\r
  this workflow is adapted from; linked above).\r
- Neavin *et al.* (2024), *Genome Biology* — **Demuxafy**, the downstream\r
  demultiplexing framework these SNP profiles feed.\r
- The reference panels and tools above per their own citation requirements\r
  (1000 Genomes Project; Minimac4; Eagle; plink; bcftools; GenotypeHarmonizer;\r
  CrossMap).\r
\r
See `CITATION.cff` for how to cite this workflow itself.\r
\r
## Running\r
\r
Each stage has a driver script that runs from the top of a super-project that\r
mounts this repo as a module (see\r
[brca_mega_atlas-data](https://github.com/swarbricklab/brca_mega_atlas-data)):\r
\r
```bash\r
./modules/imputation/run_qc.sh           # QC stage\r
./modules/imputation/run_imputation.sh   # imputation stage\r
```\r
\r
On NCI the driver uses the shared PBS profile carried as a nested submodule\r
(`profiles/global` → `swarbricklab/snakemake_config`). Check the repo out\r
recursively:\r
\r
```bash\r
git submodule update --init --recursive\r
```\r
\r
## Status\r
\r
Public, citable (`CITATION.cff`), and reproducible from public inputs — ready for the\r
**v1.0.0** release. Runs are deterministic: reruns from identical inputs are byte-identical.\r
Deliberate divergences from the upstream\r
sc-eQTLGen pipeline are documented in `docs/UPSTREAM_DIFFERENCES.md`; planned\r
post-1.0 improvements are tracked in the\r
[issue tracker](https://github.com/swarbricklab/imputation/issues).\r
""" ;
