\r
# Description\r
Matrix multiplication is a binary operation that takes a pair of matrices and produces another matrix.\r
\r
If A is an n×m matrix and B is an m×p matrix, the result AB of their multiplication is an n×p matrix defined only if the number of columns m in A is equal to the number of rows m in B. When multiplying A and B, the elements of the rows in A are multiplied with corresponding columns in B.\r
\r
In this implementation, A and B are square matrices (same number of rows and columns), and so it is the result matrix C. Each matrix is divided in N blocks of M doubles (N hardcoded to 2, and M hardcoded to 8). The multiplication of two blocks is done by a multiply task method with a simple three-nested-loop implementation. When executed with COMPSs, the main program generates N^3^ tasks arranged as N^2^ chains of N tasks in the dependency graph.\r
\r
# Reproducibility\r
To reproduce the exact results of this example, follow the instructions at the [Workflow Provenance section at COMPSs User Manual](https://compss-doc.readthedocs.io/en/stable/Sections/05_Tools/04_Workflow_Provenance.html), WITHOUT data persistence, PyCOMPSs application.\r
\r
# Execution instructions\r
Usage:\r
```\r
runcompss --lang=python src/matmul_files.py inputs_folder/ outputs_folder/\r
```\r
\r
where:\r
* inputs_folder/: Folder where A and B matrices are located\r
* outputs_folder/: Folder with the resulting C matrix\r
\r
\r
# Execution Examples\r
```\r
runcompss --lang=python src/matmul_files.py inputs/ outputs/\r
runcompss src/matmul_files.py inputs/ outputs/\r
python -m pycompss src/matmul_files.py inputs/ outputs/\r
```\r
\r
# Build\r
No build is required\r
