<https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/889?version=2> a ns1:ComputationalWorkflow ;
    dcterms:conformsTo "https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalWorkflow/1.0-RELEASE" ;
    ns1:applicationSubCategory <http://edamontology.org/topic_3168> ;
    ns1:citation "" ;
    ns1:creator "Tim Booth" ;
    ns1:dateCreated "2024-09-11" ;
    ns1:dateModified "2026-05-13" ;
    ns1:description """# pod5_by_pore\r
\r
A Snakemake workflow to take the POD5 files produced by an Oxford Nanopore sequencing run and\r
re-batch them by pore (ie. by channel).\r
\r
This is useful if you want to run duplex basecalling because you can meaningfully run\r
"dorado duplex" on a single (or a subset of) the POD5 files.\r
\r
## Know issues\r
\r
It is assumed all POD5 input files are from the same sequencing run, but this is not checked.\r
""" ;
